window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/owner-courses/b103-7eaad7f13d92709a.json"]={sha256:"7eaad7f13d92709a6e6c66ac1ef368dd265cd10b2ca520522ad6bfdbbe0935ff",value:{"id":"b103","category":"underground","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","depth":4,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-geology","v7-gotthard-construction","v7-gotthard-technical","v10-other-vendor-b103","v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"title":"哥達基線隧道","titleEn":"Gotthard Base Tunnel","summary":"沿 24 個判讀步驟研究阿爾卑斯基線鐵路的路線、地質、施工物流、防水與鐵路系統整合；以可查證的證據代替想像中的挖掘配方。","summaryEn":"Study alignment, geology, construction logistics, waterproofing and railway integration of an Alpine base tunnel through 24 evidence-led exercises.","scope":"以公開一次資料為背景的原創工程判讀課程；每步在紙上或數位示意模型中完成。自設數值、構形與工序不得當成原工程的設計、施工、設備操作或驗收程序。","scopeEn":"Original engineering interpretation exercises grounded in public primary sources. Complete each step on paper or in a schematic digital model. Invented values, geometry and sequences are not the original project’s design, construction, operating or acceptance procedures.","diagram":{"type":"tunnel","labels":["需求與場址","結構與介面","施工狀態","驗證與維護"],"labelsEn":["Requirements and site","Structures and interfaces","Construction states","Verification and maintenance"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stepCount":64,"estimatedMinutes":1600,"stages":[{"id":"b103-stage01","order":1,"title":"路線、地質與不確定性","titleEn":"Alignment, geology and uncertainty","description":"以六個相互銜接的練習完成「路線、地質與不確定性」，保留假設、圖示與判讀證據。","descriptionEn":"Complete six connected exercises on alignment, geology and uncertainty, retaining assumptions, diagrams and evidence.","steps":[{"id":"b103-v7-01","sequence":1,"order":1,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","v7-gotthard-geology","v7-gotthard-construction"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"把基線路線放回鐵路網","titleEn":"Place the base alignment in its network","objective":"理解隧道長度以外的運輸目的。","objectiveEn":"Understand the transport purpose beyond tunnel length.","instruction":"1. 畫跨山舊線與概念基線；2. 分列坡度、距離及連接路段；3. 指出一個仍可能限制全線容量的外部瓶頸。","instructionEn":"1. Sketch the mountain route and conceptual base route; 2. separate gradient, distance and connecting sections; 3. identify an external bottleneck that could still limit capacity.","observation":"隧道本身能力提高不會自動消除連接鐵路的瓶頸。","observationEn":"Improved tunnel capability does not automatically remove bottlenecks on connecting railways.","failure":"只要隧道更長就一定使整條運輸走廊更有效率。","failureEn":"A longer tunnel necessarily makes the entire transport corridor more efficient.","check":"繳交含兩端連接線的需求圖。","checkEn":"Provide a requirements map including both connecting routes.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v7-01-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"基線路線以較低高程穿越山體，坡度及路線條件影響列車牽引與運輸安排。","textEn":"A base route crosses at a lower elevation; gradients and alignment affect traction and transport planning."},{"id":"b103-v7-01-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"官方長度及運輸背景是比較起點，不能直接用來計算今天的班表能力。","textEn":"Official length and transport context begin the comparison but do not directly determine present timetable capacity."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「把基線路線放回鐵路網」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Place the base alignment in its network”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["隧道本身能力提高不會自動消除連接鐵路的瓶頸。","只要隧道更長就一定使整條運輸走廊更有效率。","增加一段隧道的能力就保證所有連接路段同步增加能力。"],"optionsEn":["Improved tunnel capability does not automatically remove bottlenecks on connecting railways.","A longer tunnel necessarily makes the entire transport corridor more efficient.","Increasing one tunnel’s capacity guarantees matching gains on all connecting routes."],"answer":0,"explanation":"基線路線以較低高程穿越山體，坡度及路線條件影響列車牽引與運輸安排。 官方長度及運輸背景是比較起點，不能直接用來計算今天的班表能力。","explanationEn":"A base route crosses at a lower elevation; gradients and alignment affect traction and transport planning. Official length and transport context begin the comparison but do not directly determine present timetable capacity."}},{"id":"b103-v7-02","sequence":2,"order":2,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","v7-gotthard-geology","v7-gotthard-construction"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v7-01"],"title":"分開雙管與連通設施","titleEn":"Separate running tubes and connections","objective":"辨認列車路徑與橫向連通功能。","objectiveEn":"Distinguish train paths from transverse connections.","instruction":"1. 畫兩條單線主隧道；2. 用不同符號標示橫坑及多功能區；3. 分開列車通道與人員通行的概念圖例。","instructionEn":"1. Draw two single-track running tubes; 2. mark cross-passages and multifunction areas with different symbols; 3. separate train paths from conceptual pedestrian connections.","observation":"兩條主隧道與橫坑具有不同功能，不能都視為可行車路線。","observationEn":"Running tubes and cross-passages have different functions and are not all train routes.","failure":"圖上只要連通就能讓列車任意從一管換到另一管。","failureEn":"Any connection drawn between tubes permits trains to change tubes there.","check":"提供至少三種連通功能的圖例。","checkEn":"Provide a legend distinguishing at least three connection functions.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v7-02-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"交通路徑、設備空間與逃生連通各有不同幾何及系統需求。","textEn":"Traffic paths, equipment spaces and escape connections have different geometric and system requirements."},{"id":"b103-v7-02-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"示意圖的連線不等於具備軌道、控制或可使用狀態。","textEn":"A connecting line in a schematic does not establish track, control or availability."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「分開雙管與連通設施」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Separate running tubes and connections”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["圖上只要連通就能讓列車任意從一管換到另一管。","兩條主隧道與橫坑具有不同功能，不能都視為可行車路線。","所有橫坑都具有列車軌道及轉轍功能。"],"optionsEn":["Any connection drawn between tubes permits trains to change tubes there.","Running tubes and cross-passages have different functions and are not all train routes.","Every cross-passage contains tracks and train-switching functions."],"answer":1,"explanation":"交通路徑、設備空間與逃生連通各有不同幾何及系統需求。 示意圖的連線不等於具備軌道、控制或可使用狀態。","explanationEn":"Traffic paths, equipment spaces and escape connections have different geometric and system requirements. A connecting line in a schematic does not establish track, control or availability."}},{"id":"b103-v7-03","sequence":3,"order":3,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","v7-gotthard-geology","v7-gotthard-construction"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v7-02"],"title":"建立地質預測與實證兩欄","titleEn":"Separate predicted geology from observations","objective":"把地質模型當成需持續更新的假說。","objectiveEn":"Treat the geological model as a hypothesis requiring updates.","instruction":"1. 畫含三種自設岩性區的縱斷面；2. 另列鑽孔與掌子面觀察欄；3. 將未驗證區段以虛線保留。","instructionEn":"1. Draw a longitudinal section with three hypothetical rock zones; 2. separate borehole and face observations; 3. keep unverified sections dashed.","observation":"地質預測必須隨新觀察更新，不能等同沿線已完全確認。","observationEn":"Geological predictions need updating with observations and do not establish complete route knowledge.","failure":"已有一張縱斷面就表示兩個鑽孔之間的岩體全部已證實。","failureEn":"One section drawing verifies every rock volume between two boreholes.","check":"提交預測、觀察與信心水準分開的剖面。","checkEn":"Submit a section separating predictions, observations and confidence.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v7-03-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"鑽孔只直接觀察有限空間，向外延伸的解釋具有不確定性。","textEn":"Boreholes directly sample limited space; extrapolated interpretations carry uncertainty."},{"id":"b103-v7-03-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"工程判讀重點是預測與實際差異如何影響模型，而非把地層畫得整齊。","textEn":"Engineering interpretation asks how prediction–observation differences affect the model, not how tidy the strata look."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「建立地質預測與實證兩欄」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Separate predicted geology from observations”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["已有一張縱斷面就表示兩個鑽孔之間的岩體全部已證實。","鑽孔間的地層圖是直接觀察全部地下空間的紀錄。","地質預測必須隨新觀察更新，不能等同沿線已完全確認。"],"optionsEn":["One section drawing verifies every rock volume between two boreholes.","A section between boreholes directly records the entire underground volume.","Geological predictions need updating with observations and do not establish complete route knowledge."],"answer":2,"explanation":"鑽孔只直接觀察有限空間，向外延伸的解釋具有不確定性。 工程判讀重點是預測與實際差異如何影響模型，而非把地層畫得整齊。","explanationEn":"Boreholes directly sample limited space; extrapolated interpretations carry uncertainty. Engineering interpretation asks how prediction–observation differences affect the model, not how tidy the strata look."}},{"id":"b103-v7-04","sequence":4,"order":4,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","v7-gotthard-geology","v7-gotthard-construction"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v7-03"],"title":"解讀斷層與破碎帶","titleEn":"Interpret faults and fractured zones","objective":"辨識岩石種類與岩體結構的不同。","objectiveEn":"Distinguish rock type from rock-mass structure.","instruction":"1. 用同一岩性畫完整及節理密集兩模型；2. 標出節理方向與水的可能路徑；3. 比較需要補充的觀察資料。","instructionEn":"1. Draw intact and heavily jointed examples of the same rock type; 2. mark joint directions and possible water paths; 3. compare required observations.","observation":"相同岩石名稱可能對應不同節理、水文及變形條件。","observationEn":"The same rock name may conceal different jointing, groundwater and deformation conditions.","failure":"只知道岩石硬度即可選定所有支護需求。","failureEn":"Rock hardness alone determines every support requirement.","check":"繳交岩性、構造與含水條件的分欄表。","checkEn":"Provide separate fields for lithology, structure and groundwater.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v7-04-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"岩體行為不只由完整岩塊強度決定，也受不連續面與水影響。","textEn":"Rock-mass behavior depends on discontinuities and water as well as intact-rock strength."},{"id":"b103-v7-04-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"本步不提供支護尺寸或挖掘設定，而是建立需由地質證據回答的問題。","textEn":"This step gives no support dimensions or excavation settings; it defines questions requiring geological evidence."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「解讀斷層與破碎帶」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Interpret faults and fractured zones”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["相同岩石名稱可能對應不同節理、水文及變形條件。","只知道岩石硬度即可選定所有支護需求。","完整岩塊的強度可以取代節理與地下水資料。"],"optionsEn":["The same rock name may conceal different jointing, groundwater and deformation conditions.","Rock hardness alone determines every support requirement.","Intact-rock strength replaces joint and groundwater information."],"answer":0,"explanation":"岩體行為不只由完整岩塊強度決定，也受不連續面與水影響。 本步不提供支護尺寸或挖掘設定，而是建立需由地質證據回答的問題。","explanationEn":"Rock-mass behavior depends on discontinuities and water as well as intact-rock strength. This step gives no support dimensions or excavation settings; it defines questions requiring geological evidence."}},{"id":"b103-v7-05","sequence":5,"order":5,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","v7-gotthard-geology","v7-gotthard-construction"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v7-04"],"title":"辨認覆土、地應力與溫度","titleEn":"Distinguish cover, stress and temperature","objective":"避免用單一深度數字概括地下條件。","objectiveEn":"Avoid reducing underground conditions to one depth number.","instruction":"1. 在斷面分別標示地表及隧道標高；2. 畫假想覆土變化；3. 將應力、熱與地下水證據列成不同需求。","instructionEn":"1. Mark surface and tunnel elevations separately; 2. draw hypothetical cover variation; 3. list separate stress, heat and groundwater evidence needs.","observation":"覆土深度增加不等於所有位置具有同樣應力方向或水壓。","observationEn":"Greater cover does not imply identical stress directions or water pressures everywhere.","failure":"地表到隧道的距離可以直接替代完整地應力與水文資料。","failureEn":"Surface-to-tunnel distance replaces complete stress and hydrogeological information.","check":"提交三類環境條件及各自需量測的資料。","checkEn":"Submit three environmental conditions with their measurement needs.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v7-05-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"地形、構造歷史與岩體性質會使應力場偏離簡單垂直自重估算。","textEn":"Topography, tectonic history and rock properties can make stress fields differ from simple overburden estimates."},{"id":"b103-v7-05-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"熱、水與力學資料具有不同量測方法，不能因共用一張剖面就互相代替。","textEn":"Thermal, hydraulic and mechanical conditions require different observations despite sharing a section drawing."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「辨認覆土、地應力與溫度」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Distinguish cover, stress and temperature”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["地表到隧道的距離可以直接替代完整地應力與水文資料。","覆土深度增加不等於所有位置具有同樣應力方向或水壓。","熱環境與水壓可從覆土深度唯一決定。"],"optionsEn":["Surface-to-tunnel distance replaces complete stress and hydrogeological information.","Greater cover does not imply identical stress directions or water pressures everywhere.","Cover depth uniquely determines temperature and water pressure."],"answer":1,"explanation":"地形、構造歷史與岩體性質會使應力場偏離簡單垂直自重估算。 熱、水與力學資料具有不同量測方法，不能因共用一張剖面就互相代替。","explanationEn":"Topography, tectonic history and rock properties can make stress fields differ from simple overburden estimates. Thermal, hydraulic and mechanical conditions require different observations despite sharing a section drawing."}},{"id":"b103-v7-06","sequence":6,"order":6,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","v7-gotthard-geology","v7-gotthard-construction"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v7-05"],"title":"制定勘察更新的決策紀錄","titleEn":"Create an investigation-update decision record","objective":"讓新地質證據影響後續模型。","objectiveEn":"Make new geological evidence propagate into downstream models.","instruction":"1. 設定一個與預測不同的假想觀察；2. 列出受影響的支護、物流與防水問題；3. 標記哪些結論需重做而哪些仍有效。","instructionEn":"1. Introduce a hypothetical observation inconsistent with prediction; 2. list affected support, logistics and waterproofing questions; 3. mark conclusions needing revision and those still valid.","observation":"新證據的價值在修正相依判斷，不能只新增一張地質照片。","observationEn":"New evidence should revise dependent judgments rather than merely add a geological photograph.","failure":"把差異記錄存檔後即可繼續沿用全部舊假設。","failureEn":"Filing a discrepancy permits all old assumptions to remain unchanged.","check":"繳交一份有上游證據及下游影響的變更單。","checkEn":"Provide a change record linking upstream evidence to downstream impacts.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v7-06-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"觀測與決策之間需要明確連結，否則資料很多也無法降低模型風險。","textEn":"Observations need explicit links to decisions; more data alone do not reduce modeling risk."},{"id":"b103-v7-06-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"未知條件可導致暫停判斷與補資料，這是工程品質控制的一部分。","textEn":"Unknown conditions can require pausing a judgment and gathering evidence as part of quality control."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「制定勘察更新的決策紀錄」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Create an investigation-update decision record”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["把差異記錄存檔後即可繼續沿用全部舊假設。","地質模型一旦發布就不應因新觀察而修改。","新證據的價值在修正相依判斷，不能只新增一張地質照片。"],"optionsEn":["Filing a discrepancy permits all old assumptions to remain unchanged.","A published geological model should never change after new observations.","New evidence should revise dependent judgments rather than merely add a geological photograph."],"answer":2,"explanation":"觀測與決策之間需要明確連結，否則資料很多也無法降低模型風險。 未知條件可導致暫停判斷與補資料，這是工程品質控制的一部分。","explanationEn":"Observations need explicit links to decisions; more data alone do not reduce modeling risk. Unknown conditions can require pausing a judgment and gathering evidence as part of quality control."}}]},{"id":"b103-stage02","order":2,"title":"開挖狀態與施工物流","titleEn":"Excavation states and logistics","description":"以六個相互銜接的練習完成「開挖狀態與施工物流」，保留假設、圖示與判讀證據。","descriptionEn":"Complete six connected exercises on excavation states and logistics, retaining assumptions, diagrams and evidence.","steps":[{"id":"b103-v7-07","sequence":7,"order":1,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","v7-gotthard-geology","v7-gotthard-construction"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v7-06"],"title":"比較機械掘進與分部開挖概念","titleEn":"Compare mechanized and staged excavation concepts","objective":"理解工法選擇取決於地質、斷面與物流。","objectiveEn":"Understand that methods depend on ground, geometry and logistics.","instruction":"1. 畫機械掘進與分部開挖的概念狀態；2. 比較斷面自由度、設備空間及出碴介面；3. 列出不能從照片推定的條件。","instructionEn":"1. Sketch mechanized and staged excavation concepts; 2. compare geometric flexibility, equipment space and muck interfaces; 3. list conditions that photographs cannot establish.","observation":"設備外觀相似不代表不同地質區段可沿用同一作業設定。","observationEn":"Similar equipment appearance does not justify identical settings in different ground.","failure":"只要使用最大掘進機就能解決所有地質問題。","failureEn":"The largest tunnel-boring machine solves every geological problem.","check":"提交三個工法比較維度與各自資料缺口。","checkEn":"Submit three method-comparison dimensions with evidence gaps.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v7-07-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"施工方法是系統選擇，需要處理掌子面、支護、設備與物流的相容性。","textEn":"An excavation method is a system choice involving compatibility among face, support, equipment and logistics."},{"id":"b103-v7-07-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"本課程不提供爆破參數或掘進機操作值，只比較公開工法機理。","textEn":"The course provides no blasting parameters or machine settings and compares only public method concepts."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「比較機械掘進與分部開挖概念」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Compare mechanized and staged excavation concepts”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["設備外觀相似不代表不同地質區段可沿用同一作業設定。","只要使用最大掘進機就能解決所有地質問題。","施工方法只取決於隧道的總長度。"],"optionsEn":["Similar equipment appearance does not justify identical settings in different ground.","The largest tunnel-boring machine solves every geological problem.","Excavation method depends only on total tunnel length."],"answer":0,"explanation":"施工方法是系統選擇，需要處理掌子面、支護、設備與物流的相容性。 本課程不提供爆破參數或掘進機操作值，只比較公開工法機理。","explanationEn":"An excavation method is a system choice involving compatibility among face, support, equipment and logistics. The course provides no blasting parameters or machine settings and compares only public method concepts."}},{"id":"b103-v7-08","sequence":8,"order":2,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","v7-gotthard-geology","v7-gotthard-construction"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v7-07"],"title":"分辨開挖面與後方工作區","titleEn":"Separate the face from trailing work zones","objective":"把掘進視為串接工序而非單一刀盤。","objectiveEn":"Treat tunnelling as a connected process rather than one cutterhead.","instruction":"1. 畫掌子面、支護及後方輸送三區；2. 標示人、材料與碴料的不同流線；3. 找出一個可能阻塞其他區的介面。","instructionEn":"1. Draw face, support and trailing-conveyor zones; 2. separate people, material and muck flows; 3. identify an interface that can block other zones.","observation":"前端掘進加快若超過後端能力，整體進度未必提高。","observationEn":"Faster advance need not improve progress when downstream capacity is insufficient.","failure":"只提高刀盤理論效率就可保證全隧道工期等比例縮短。","failureEn":"Higher theoretical cutterhead efficiency guarantees proportional schedule reduction.","check":"提交三區流線圖及一個瓶頸說明。","checkEn":"Provide a three-zone flow map and one bottleneck explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v7-08-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"串联系統的能力受限制環節影響，停機與交界等待不能在總體模型中省略。","textEn":"A serial system is constrained by limiting stages; downtime and interface waits matter to the overall model."},{"id":"b103-v7-08-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"教學流線只顯示相依關係，不是現地通行或施工配置圖。","textEn":"The teaching flow map shows dependencies, not a field traffic or construction layout."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「分辨開挖面與後方工作區」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Separate the face from trailing work zones”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["只提高刀盤理論效率就可保證全隧道工期等比例縮短。","前端掘進加快若超過後端能力，整體進度未必提高。","後方輸送能力不會限制前端掘進的總產出。"],"optionsEn":["Higher theoretical cutterhead efficiency guarantees proportional schedule reduction.","Faster advance need not improve progress when downstream capacity is insufficient.","Trailing transport capacity cannot limit overall advance output."],"answer":1,"explanation":"串联系統的能力受限制環節影響，停機與交界等待不能在總體模型中省略。 教學流線只顯示相依關係，不是現地通行或施工配置圖。","explanationEn":"A serial system is constrained by limiting stages; downtime and interface waits matter to the overall model. The teaching flow map shows dependencies, not a field traffic or construction layout."}},{"id":"b103-v7-09","sequence":9,"order":3,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","v7-gotthard-geology","v7-gotthard-construction"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v7-08"],"title":"拆出臨時支護與永久襯砌","titleEn":"Separate temporary support and final lining","objective":"辨認不同時間狀態下的承載機理。","objectiveEn":"Recognize load-resistance mechanisms at different times.","instruction":"1. 畫剛開挖、初期支護及完成襯砌三狀態；2. 記錄各狀態已存在的構件；3. 比較岩體與結構的相互作用假設。","instructionEn":"1. Draw freshly excavated, initially supported and finally lined states; 2. list components present in each; 3. compare ground–structure interaction assumptions.","observation":"永久襯砌的存在不能回頭證明未完成階段的穩定性。","observationEn":"A final lining does not retrospectively verify stability before its completion.","failure":"將完工襯砌放入所有施工狀態即可簡化而不影響判斷。","failureEn":"Adding the completed lining to every construction state simplifies analysis without consequence.","check":"提交三狀態構件與反力表。","checkEn":"Submit a table of components and reactions for three states.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v7-09-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"地下結構與岩體共同變形；支護安裝時機及邊界是模型的一部分。","textEn":"Underground structures and ground deform together; installation timing and boundaries are part of the model."},{"id":"b103-v7-09-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"概念狀態分析不能直接決定現場支護間距或施工時序。","textEn":"Conceptual state analysis cannot directly determine field support spacing or work sequence."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「拆出臨時支護與永久襯砌」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Separate temporary support and final lining”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["將完工襯砌放入所有施工狀態即可簡化而不影響判斷。","臨時支護的安裝時間不會改變岩體與結構互動。","永久襯砌的存在不能回頭證明未完成階段的穩定性。"],"optionsEn":["Adding the completed lining to every construction state simplifies analysis without consequence.","Temporary-support timing does not affect ground–structure interaction.","A final lining does not retrospectively verify stability before its completion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"地下結構與岩體共同變形；支護安裝時機及邊界是模型的一部分。 概念狀態分析不能直接決定現場支護間距或施工時序。","explanationEn":"Underground structures and ground deform together; installation timing and boundaries are part of the model. Conceptual state analysis cannot directly determine field support spacing or work sequence."}},{"id":"b103-v7-10","sequence":10,"order":4,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","v7-gotthard-geology","v7-gotthard-construction"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v7-09"],"title":"讀取收斂量測的時間曲線","titleEn":"Interpret convergence time histories","objective":"區分變形速率、總量與量測重置。","objectiveEn":"Distinguish deformation rate, total movement and datum resets.","instruction":"1. 建立三條自設收斂曲線；2. 分別加入趨穩、加速與基準跳點；3. 對每條列出下一個應查證的資料。","instructionEn":"1. Create three synthetic convergence curves; 2. include stabilization, acceleration and a datum jump; 3. specify the next evidence check for each.","observation":"曲線跳點可能來自量測基準變更，需先查紀錄再判斷岩體突變。","observationEn":"A curve jump can result from a datum change and requires record checks before inferring abrupt ground behavior.","failure":"量測跳點必然表示隧道立即發生同等變形。","failureEn":"Every measurement jump necessarily indicates equal immediate tunnel movement.","check":"繳交三曲線的候選解釋及查證表。","checkEn":"Provide candidate explanations and checks for three curves.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v7-10-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"變形量及其時間趨勢傳達不同資訊；單一讀數缺少速率與背景。","textEn":"Movement magnitude and time trend convey different information; one reading lacks rate and context."},{"id":"b103-v7-10-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"所有警戒值在本練習都保持未指定，不以自設曲線設定真實工地限值。","textEn":"Alert thresholds remain unspecified; synthetic curves do not establish real construction limits."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「讀取收斂量測的時間曲線」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Interpret convergence time histories”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["曲線跳點可能來自量測基準變更，需先查紀錄再判斷岩體突變。","量測跳點必然表示隧道立即發生同等變形。","變形總量相同就表示各曲線的速率相同。"],"optionsEn":["A curve jump can result from a datum change and requires record checks before inferring abrupt ground behavior.","Every measurement jump necessarily indicates equal immediate tunnel movement.","Equal total movement implies equal rates in every curve."],"answer":0,"explanation":"變形量及其時間趨勢傳達不同資訊；單一讀數缺少速率與背景。 所有警戒值在本練習都保持未指定，不以自設曲線設定真實工地限值。","explanationEn":"Movement magnitude and time trend convey different information; one reading lacks rate and context. Alert thresholds remain unspecified; synthetic curves do not establish real construction limits."}},{"id":"b103-v7-11","sequence":11,"order":5,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","v7-gotthard-geology","v7-gotthard-construction"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v7-10"],"title":"建立出碴與材料再利用帳","titleEn":"Create a muck and reuse ledger","objective":"追蹤材料品質、去向與物流守恆。","objectiveEn":"Track material quality, destination and logistics conservation.","instruction":"1. 對自設碴料批次建立重量欄；2. 依待檢、可用、不可用分流；3. 核對庫存變化與運出入是否平衡。","instructionEn":"1. Assign masses to hypothetical muck batches; 2. separate pending, suitable and unsuitable streams; 3. reconcile inventory with inflows and outflows.","observation":"材料數量平衡成立仍不代表每批都適合再利用。","observationEn":"A balanced material ledger does not establish suitability of every batch for reuse.","failure":"所有挖出的岩石都能直接當成同等級混凝土骨材。","failureEn":"Every excavated rock batch can directly serve as equivalent concrete aggregate.","check":"輸出有品質狀態及去向的批次守恆表。","checkEn":"Produce a batch balance with quality status and destinations.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v7-11-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"材料再利用需要性質與污染等證據，不能僅依岩石外觀決定用途。","textEn":"Reuse requires property and contamination evidence rather than appearance alone."},{"id":"b103-v7-11-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"庫存、運輸與品質結果是不同資料流，需要共同批次識別碼才能追溯。","textEn":"Inventory, transport and quality results require common batch identifiers for traceability."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「建立出碴與材料再利用帳」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Create a muck and reuse ledger”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["所有挖出的岩石都能直接當成同等級混凝土骨材。","材料數量平衡成立仍不代表每批都適合再利用。","出碴重量相同就代表所有批次具有相同材料品質。"],"optionsEn":["Every excavated rock batch can directly serve as equivalent concrete aggregate.","A balanced material ledger does not establish suitability of every batch for reuse.","Equal muck masses establish identical quality in every batch."],"answer":1,"explanation":"材料再利用需要性質與污染等證據，不能僅依岩石外觀決定用途。 庫存、運輸與品質結果是不同資料流，需要共同批次識別碼才能追溯。","explanationEn":"Reuse requires property and contamination evidence rather than appearance alone. Inventory, transport and quality results require common batch identifiers for traceability."}},{"id":"b103-v7-12","sequence":12,"order":6,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","v7-gotthard-geology","v7-gotthard-construction"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v7-11"],"title":"協調多工作面的共同介面","titleEn":"Coordinate multiple work fronts","objective":"理解平行開挖如何共享基準與資源。","objectiveEn":"Understand shared datums and resources in parallel drives.","instruction":"1. 畫兩個假想工作面與共同出入口；2. 設定共用運輸及測量介面；3. 模擬其中一區延後時的相依影響。","instructionEn":"1. Draw two hypothetical faces and a shared access; 2. define shared transport and survey interfaces; 3. trace consequences when one area is delayed.","observation":"增加工作面會增加並行能力，也可能增加共用資源衝突。","observationEn":"Additional faces increase parallel opportunities but can create shared-resource conflicts.","failure":"工作面數量加倍就一定使完工時間減半。","failureEn":"Doubling work fronts necessarily halves completion time.","check":"提交資源與基準的兩類相依圖。","checkEn":"Provide separate dependency maps for resources and datums.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v7-12-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"平行任務需共享可靠的幾何基準，否則速度提升可能累積到貫通誤差。","textEn":"Parallel tasks need reliable shared geometry or faster progress can accumulate breakthrough mismatch."},{"id":"b103-v7-12-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"施工組織比較需考慮資源限制及介面等待，不能只加總理論掘進率。","textEn":"Construction organization must consider resource limits and interface waits, not only theoretical advance rates."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「協調多工作面的共同介面」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Coordinate multiple work fronts”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["工作面數量加倍就一定使完工時間減半。","平行工作面不需共同測量基準，只需各自前進。","增加工作面會增加並行能力，也可能增加共用資源衝突。"],"optionsEn":["Doubling work fronts necessarily halves completion time.","Parallel work fronts need no shared survey datum, only local advance.","Additional faces increase parallel opportunities but can create shared-resource conflicts."],"answer":2,"explanation":"平行任務需共享可靠的幾何基準，否則速度提升可能累積到貫通誤差。 施工組織比較需考慮資源限制及介面等待，不能只加總理論掘進率。","explanationEn":"Parallel tasks need reliable shared geometry or faster progress can accumulate breakthrough mismatch. Construction organization must consider resource limits and interface waits, not only theoretical advance rates."}}]},{"id":"b103-stage03","order":3,"title":"襯砌、防水與鐵路介面","titleEn":"Lining, waterproofing and railway interfaces","description":"以六個相互銜接的練習完成「襯砌、防水與鐵路介面」，保留假設、圖示與判讀證據。","descriptionEn":"Complete six connected exercises on lining, waterproofing and railway interfaces, retaining assumptions, diagrams and evidence.","steps":[{"id":"b103-v7-13","sequence":13,"order":1,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-geology","v7-gotthard-construction","v7-gotthard-technical"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v7-12"],"title":"檢查雙向貫通的誤差鏈","titleEn":"Review breakthrough error chains","objective":"理解方向、距離與座標基準的累積。","objectiveEn":"Understand accumulation of direction, distance and reference errors.","instruction":"1. 畫兩端向中間延伸的測線；2. 加入小幅自設角度及距離偏差；3. 比較閉合差並註明同一座標基準。","instructionEn":"1. Draw survey chains advancing from opposite ends; 2. introduce small hypothetical angle and distance errors; 3. compare closure under one reference frame.","observation":"很小的方向偏差沿長距離延伸可能形成明顯橫向閉合差。","observationEn":"A small directional error over a long distance can create substantial lateral closure error.","failure":"只要每段距離量得精確就可忽略方向與座標轉換。","failureEn":"Accurate segment distances make direction and coordinate transformations irrelevant.","check":"輸出兩條誤差鏈及一份閉合差來源表。","checkEn":"Provide two error chains and a closure-error source table.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v7-13-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"測量誤差可含系統性與隨機部分，方向偏差不能用距離精度掩蓋。","textEn":"Survey errors include systematic and random components; distance precision does not hide direction bias."},{"id":"b103-v7-13-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"公開地圖座標不是隧道貫通測量基準，本步使用自設平面座標。","textEn":"Public map coordinates are not tunnel breakthrough control; this exercise uses an invented planar frame."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「檢查雙向貫通的誤差鏈」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Review breakthrough error chains”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["很小的方向偏差沿長距離延伸可能形成明顯橫向閉合差。","只要每段距離量得精確就可忽略方向與座標轉換。","測線方向偏差只影響起點，不會隨距離累積。"],"optionsEn":["A small directional error over a long distance can create substantial lateral closure error.","Accurate segment distances make direction and coordinate transformations irrelevant.","Survey-direction bias affects only the starting point and cannot accumulate with distance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"測量誤差可含系統性與隨機部分，方向偏差不能用距離精度掩蓋。 公開地圖座標不是隧道貫通測量基準，本步使用自設平面座標。","explanationEn":"Survey errors include systematic and random components; distance precision does not hide direction bias. Public map coordinates are not tunnel breakthrough control; this exercise uses an invented planar frame."}},{"id":"b103-v7-14","sequence":14,"order":2,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-geology","v7-gotthard-construction","v7-gotthard-technical"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v7-13"],"title":"分開滲水來源與排水去向","titleEn":"Separate seepage sources and drainage destinations","objective":"建立水路與結構邊界的概念模型。","objectiveEn":"Build a conceptual model of water paths and structural boundaries.","instruction":"1. 畫岩體、支護、防水層及內襯；2. 用箭頭標示假想滲水；3. 分列清水、可能污染水與未知來源。","instructionEn":"1. Draw ground, support, waterproofing and inner lining; 2. mark hypothetical seepage; 3. separate clean, potentially contaminated and unknown sources.","observation":"不同來源的水應先辨識，不能直接假設具有相同排放條件。","observationEn":"Water sources need identification before assuming identical discharge conditions.","failure":"水都是透明就能合併成同一條無需檢測的排水線。","failureEn":"All clear-looking water can share one untested discharge route.","check":"提交標示未知水源及去向的水路圖。","checkEn":"Submit a water-path diagram with unknown sources and destinations.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v7-14-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"地下水、施工用水與污染事件可能需要不同處理，外觀不足以判定品質。","textEn":"Groundwater, process water and contamination events can require different treatment; appearance is insufficient."},{"id":"b103-v7-14-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"防水與排水需協調，堵住可見水路不一定解決上游壓力問題。","textEn":"Waterproofing and drainage must be coordinated; blocking visible flow does not necessarily address upstream pressure."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「分開滲水來源與排水去向」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Separate seepage sources and drainage destinations”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["水都是透明就能合併成同一條無需檢測的排水線。","不同來源的水應先辨識，不能直接假設具有相同排放條件。","封住可見漏水就能保證上游水壓也消失。"],"optionsEn":["All clear-looking water can share one untested discharge route.","Water sources need identification before assuming identical discharge conditions.","Blocking visible leakage guarantees upstream water pressure disappears."],"answer":1,"explanation":"地下水、施工用水與污染事件可能需要不同處理，外觀不足以判定品質。 防水與排水需協調，堵住可見水路不一定解決上游壓力問題。","explanationEn":"Groundwater, process water and contamination events can require different treatment; appearance is insufficient. Waterproofing and drainage must be coordinated; blocking visible flow does not necessarily address upstream pressure."}},{"id":"b103-v7-15","sequence":15,"order":3,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-geology","v7-gotthard-construction","v7-gotthard-technical"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v7-14"],"title":"核對襯砌接縫與連通口","titleEn":"Check lining joints and connection openings","objective":"把局部細節視為連續系統的弱點候選。","objectiveEn":"Treat local details as potential discontinuities in a continuous system.","instruction":"1. 畫襯砌、接縫與橫坑開口；2. 標記水、力及電纜三種跨界路徑；3. 列出各自需保留的施工與檢查紀錄。","instructionEn":"1. Draw lining, joints and a cross-passage opening; 2. mark water, force and cable crossings; 3. list installation and inspection records for each.","observation":"連續壁面模型不能自動代表接縫與穿透部位的行為。","observationEn":"A continuous-wall model does not automatically represent joints and penetrations.","failure":"大部分襯砌沒有滲水就能證明每個接縫都具有相同品質。","failureEn":"A mostly dry lining proves identical quality at every joint.","check":"輸出至少三種跨界介面的證據清單。","checkEn":"Provide evidence lists for at least three crossing interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v7-15-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"幾何不連續會改變局部變形、水路及應力分布，因此需要具體細節資料。","textEn":"Geometric discontinuities change local deformation, flow and stresses and require detail-specific evidence."},{"id":"b103-v7-15-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"照片與示意圖有助於定位，但不能代替隱蔽工程及材料紀錄。","textEn":"Photos and schematics locate details but do not replace concealed-work and material records."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「核對襯砌接縫與連通口」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Check lining joints and connection openings”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["大部分襯砌沒有滲水就能證明每個接縫都具有相同品質。","整段襯砌看似連續即可刪除接縫與開口模型。","連續壁面模型不能自動代表接縫與穿透部位的行為。"],"optionsEn":["A mostly dry lining proves identical quality at every joint.","An apparently continuous lining permits deletion of joint and opening models.","A continuous-wall model does not automatically represent joints and penetrations."],"answer":2,"explanation":"幾何不連續會改變局部變形、水路及應力分布，因此需要具體細節資料。 照片與示意圖有助於定位，但不能代替隱蔽工程及材料紀錄。","explanationEn":"Geometric discontinuities change local deformation, flow and stresses and require detail-specific evidence. Photos and schematics locate details but do not replace concealed-work and material records."}},{"id":"b103-v7-16","sequence":16,"order":4,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-geology","v7-gotthard-construction","v7-gotthard-technical"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v7-15"],"title":"把軌道幾何連到結構空間","titleEn":"Connect track geometry to structural space","objective":"辨識行車界限、軌道基準與維修空間。","objectiveEn":"Distinguish vehicle clearance, track datums and maintenance space.","instruction":"1. 在隧道斷面畫概念軌道及車輛包絡；2. 另畫架空線與走道；3. 比較軌道偏移對各介面空間的影響。","instructionEn":"1. Draw conceptual track and vehicle envelopes; 2. add overhead equipment and walkways; 3. compare effects of track offsets on interface space.","observation":"隧道淨空合適仍需核對軌道位置與設備包絡的共同條件。","observationEn":"Adequate tunnel size still requires compatible track position and equipment envelopes.","failure":"土建斷面容得下車體就代表全部鐵路設備都可直接安裝。","failureEn":"A civil section containing the vehicle body guarantees fit for all railway equipment.","check":"提供三種包絡及共同基準的斷面圖。","checkEn":"Provide a section with three envelopes and a common datum.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v7-16-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"土建及鐵路設備使用同一幾何空間，但各自有安裝、運動與維護需求。","textEn":"Civil works and railway equipment share space but have distinct installation, movement and maintenance needs."},{"id":"b103-v7-16-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"本步包絡為教學自繪，不提供真實鐵路通行或設備淨空批准值。","textEn":"Teaching envelopes are original sketches, not approved railway or equipment-clearance values."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「把軌道幾何連到結構空間」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Connect track geometry to structural space”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["隧道淨空合適仍需核對軌道位置與設備包絡的共同條件。","土建斷面容得下車體就代表全部鐵路設備都可直接安裝。","車輛包絡與設備維修包絡永遠相同。"],"optionsEn":["Adequate tunnel size still requires compatible track position and equipment envelopes.","A civil section containing the vehicle body guarantees fit for all railway equipment.","Vehicle and equipment-maintenance envelopes are always identical."],"answer":0,"explanation":"土建及鐵路設備使用同一幾何空間，但各自有安裝、運動與維護需求。 本步包絡為教學自繪，不提供真實鐵路通行或設備淨空批准值。","explanationEn":"Civil works and railway equipment share space but have distinct installation, movement and maintenance needs. Teaching envelopes are original sketches, not approved railway or equipment-clearance values."}},{"id":"b103-v7-17","sequence":17,"order":5,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-geology","v7-gotthard-construction","v7-gotthard-technical"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v7-16"],"title":"區分供電、通訊與控制介面","titleEn":"Separate power, communications and control","objective":"理解鐵路營運是多系統整合。","objectiveEn":"Understand railway operation as multisystem integration.","instruction":"1. 畫供電、通訊與列車控制三條功能鏈；2. 標示資訊及能源流向；3. 列出中斷任一鏈時需要查證的狀態。","instructionEn":"1. Draw power, communications and train-control chains; 2. distinguish information and energy flows; 3. list states needing verification if one chain is interrupted.","observation":"通訊連通並不單獨證明電力或列車控制功能可用。","observationEn":"Communication connectivity alone does not establish power or train-control availability.","failure":"所有設備都回應網路訊息就可判定隧道已具備行車條件。","failureEn":"Network responses from every device establish train-operating readiness.","check":"提交三條功能鏈及至少三個交界問題。","checkEn":"Submit three functional chains and at least three interface questions.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v7-17-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"子系統可用與系統整合可用是不同層級，必須對應到服務功能。","textEn":"Subsystem availability and integrated readiness are different levels and must map to service functions."},{"id":"b103-v7-17-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"課程只討論功能邊界，不提供真實列車控制配置或現地操作指令。","textEn":"The course discusses functional boundaries, not actual train-control configurations or field commands."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「區分供電、通訊與控制介面」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Separate power, communications and control”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["所有設備都回應網路訊息就可判定隧道已具備行車條件。","通訊連通並不單獨證明電力或列車控制功能可用。","能源流與資訊流可用同一條線不加區分地驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Network responses from every device establish train-operating readiness.","Communication connectivity alone does not establish power or train-control availability.","Energy and information flows can be verified as one indistinguishable line."],"answer":1,"explanation":"子系統可用與系統整合可用是不同層級，必須對應到服務功能。 課程只討論功能邊界，不提供真實列車控制配置或現地操作指令。","explanationEn":"Subsystem availability and integrated readiness are different levels and must map to service functions. The course discusses functional boundaries, not actual train-control configurations or field commands."}},{"id":"b103-v7-18","sequence":18,"order":6,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-geology","v7-gotthard-construction","v7-gotthard-technical"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v7-17"],"title":"建立土建移交的證據索引","titleEn":"Create a civil-to-systems handover index","objective":"防止已完工與已適合安裝的概念混淆。","objectiveEn":"Avoid conflating construction completion with installation readiness.","instruction":"1. 列出斷面、滲水、基準及預留介面；2. 為每項配一種紀錄與版本；3. 標記尚未解決、會阻礙設備安裝的缺項。","instructionEn":"1. List geometry, seepage, datums and reserved interfaces; 2. assign a record and version to each; 3. flag unresolved items preventing installation readiness.","observation":"土建完成日期不是每個機電介面已驗證的替代證據。","observationEn":"A civil completion date does not substitute for verified service interfaces.","failure":"開挖貫通就表示所有後續安裝與營運驗證都已完成。","failureEn":"Breakthrough means all installation and operational verification are complete.","check":"繳交可追到位置及版本的移交索引。","checkEn":"Submit a handover index traceable to location and version.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v7-18-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"移交將幾何、品質及限制資訊交給下一專業，是功能整合的一部分。","textEn":"Handover transfers geometry, quality and limitations to the next discipline as part of functional integration."},{"id":"b103-v7-18-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"證據應明確標示驗證範圍，不能把一段合格延伸為全線合格。","textEn":"Evidence must state verified scope rather than extend one accepted section to the whole route."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「建立土建移交的證據索引」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Create a civil-to-systems handover index”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["開挖貫通就表示所有後續安裝與營運驗證都已完成。","移交只需要完成日期，不需要資料位置與版本。","土建完成日期不是每個機電介面已驗證的替代證據。"],"optionsEn":["Breakthrough means all installation and operational verification are complete.","Handover needs only a completion date, not data location and version.","A civil completion date does not substitute for verified service interfaces."],"answer":2,"explanation":"移交將幾何、品質及限制資訊交給下一專業，是功能整合的一部分。 證據應明確標示驗證範圍，不能把一段合格延伸為全線合格。","explanationEn":"Handover transfers geometry, quality and limitations to the next discipline as part of functional integration. Evidence must state verified scope rather than extend one accepted section to the whole route."}}]},{"id":"b103-stage04","order":4,"title":"系統驗證與衍生工程","titleEn":"System verification and related projects","description":"以六個相互銜接的練習完成「系統驗證與衍生工程」，保留假設、圖示與判讀證據。","descriptionEn":"Complete six connected exercises on system verification and related projects, retaining assumptions, diagrams and evidence.","steps":[{"id":"b103-v7-19","sequence":19,"order":1,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-geology","v7-gotthard-construction","v7-gotthard-technical"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v7-18"],"title":"分開局部試驗與整合試驗","titleEn":"Separate local and integrated tests","objective":"建立從設備功能到服務功能的證據鏈。","objectiveEn":"Build an evidence chain from device function to service function.","instruction":"1. 為一個概念通訊節點列出局部測試；2. 加入跨區端到端情境；3. 標記局部通過仍無法回答的整體問題。","instructionEn":"1. Define a local test for a conceptual communication node; 2. add an end-to-end cross-zone scenario; 3. identify system questions not answered by local success.","observation":"各設備單獨通過並不保證跨系統的功能與時序相容。","observationEn":"Independent device passes do not establish compatible cross-system functions and timing.","failure":"把各廠商測試報告相加即可取代所有整合驗證。","failureEn":"Adding supplier reports replaces every integration test.","check":"提交要求、測試範圍及缺口三欄矩陣。","checkEn":"Provide a requirements, test-scope and gap matrix.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v7-19-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"整合驗證針對介面與共同情境，與單體功能試驗具有不同覆蓋範圍。","textEn":"Integration verification covers interfaces and shared scenarios distinct from standalone function tests."},{"id":"b103-v7-19-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"自設案例用於查漏，不宣稱重現哥達隧道的正式驗收程序。","textEn":"Synthetic cases expose gaps and do not reproduce Gotthard’s formal acceptance process."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「分開局部試驗與整合試驗」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Separate local and integrated tests”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["各設備單獨通過並不保證跨系統的功能與時序相容。","把各廠商測試報告相加即可取代所有整合驗證。","整合試驗只是單體試驗更換名稱，覆蓋範圍完全相同。"],"optionsEn":["Independent device passes do not establish compatible cross-system functions and timing.","Adding supplier reports replaces every integration test.","Integration testing merely renames component testing with identical coverage."],"answer":0,"explanation":"整合驗證針對介面與共同情境，與單體功能試驗具有不同覆蓋範圍。 自設案例用於查漏，不宣稱重現哥達隧道的正式驗收程序。","explanationEn":"Integration verification covers interfaces and shared scenarios distinct from standalone function tests. Synthetic cases expose gaps and do not reproduce Gotthard’s formal acceptance process."}},{"id":"b103-v7-20","sequence":20,"order":2,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-geology","v7-gotthard-construction","v7-gotthard-technical"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v7-19"],"title":"用非操作方式檢查可達性","titleEn":"Review access without issuing operating instructions","objective":"辨識平面連通與實際可使用的差異。","objectiveEn":"Distinguish drawn connectivity from practical availability.","instruction":"1. 在雙管圖標出概念人員路徑；2. 另列門、照明及資訊需求；3. 以缺少一項資訊的例子說明不能直接判定可達。","instructionEn":"1. Mark conceptual pedestrian routes on the twin-tube diagram; 2. list door, lighting and information needs; 3. show why one missing item prevents an availability judgment.","observation":"圖上路徑連通仍需設備、資訊與狀態證據才能判斷可使用。","observationEn":"A connected path still requires equipment, information and state evidence before judging usability.","failure":"橫坑存在就自動代表任何情境下都可自由通行。","failureEn":"The existence of a cross-passage implies free passage in every scenario.","check":"提交功能需求清單，保留現地程序為未提供。","checkEn":"Submit functional requirements while leaving field procedures unspecified.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v7-20-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"可達性包含幾何與狀態；一條線無法表達門、環境及設備可用性。","textEn":"Access includes geometry and state; one line cannot represent doors, environment and equipment availability."},{"id":"b103-v7-20-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"本練習不提供火災、疏散或列車事故處置程序，實務須遵循營運者指引。","textEn":"This exercise supplies no fire, evacuation or train-incident procedure; actual practice follows operator guidance."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「用非操作方式檢查可達性」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Review access without issuing operating instructions”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["橫坑存在就自動代表任何情境下都可自由通行。","圖上路徑連通仍需設備、資訊與狀態證據才能判斷可使用。","一張平面圖可完整表達門的狀態、照明及設備可用性。"],"optionsEn":["The existence of a cross-passage implies free passage in every scenario.","A connected path still requires equipment, information and state evidence before judging usability.","One plan fully represents door states, lighting and equipment availability."],"answer":1,"explanation":"可達性包含幾何與狀態；一條線無法表達門、環境及設備可用性。 本練習不提供火災、疏散或列車事故處置程序，實務須遵循營運者指引。","explanationEn":"Access includes geometry and state; one line cannot represent doors, environment and equipment availability. This exercise supplies no fire, evacuation or train-incident procedure; actual practice follows operator guidance."}},{"id":"b103-v7-21","sequence":21,"order":3,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-geology","v7-gotthard-construction","v7-gotthard-technical"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v7-20"],"title":"建立維護窗口的介面問題","titleEn":"Map maintenance-window interface questions","objective":"辨識單一設備維修與鐵路服務之間的依賴。","objectiveEn":"Identify dependencies between equipment maintenance and railway service.","instruction":"1. 選一個假想設備維護項；2. 標出共用供電、通訊及接近路徑；3. 區分設備完成、功能複核及服務恢復三種狀態。","instructionEn":"1. Select a hypothetical equipment-maintenance task; 2. mark shared power, communications and access paths; 3. distinguish task completion, functional recheck and service restoration.","observation":"維修工作結束與整個相關功能已恢復是不同的證據判斷。","observationEn":"Finishing a maintenance task and restoring the associated integrated function are different evidence judgments.","failure":"單一設備修好就能自行判定所有相關鐵路服務已恢復。","failureEn":"Repairing one device independently establishes that every related railway service has been restored.","check":"提交三種狀態及交界證據的相依圖。","checkEn":"Submit a dependency map of three states and interface evidence.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v7-21-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"共享資源會使維護影響跨越單一設備邊界，因此應追蹤相關功能。","textEn":"Shared resources let maintenance effects cross device boundaries, so related functions must be traced."},{"id":"b103-v7-21-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"課程只建立工程問題，不指定封鎖、隔離、復電或列車營運程序。","textEn":"The exercise defines engineering questions and specifies no possession, isolation, reenergization or train-operating procedure."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「建立維護窗口的介面問題」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Map maintenance-window interface questions”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["單一設備修好就能自行判定所有相關鐵路服務已恢復。","共用資源只影響被維護的設備，不會影響相鄰功能。","維修工作結束與整個相關功能已恢復是不同的證據判斷。"],"optionsEn":["Repairing one device independently establishes that every related railway service has been restored.","Shared resources affect only maintained equipment and never adjacent functions.","Finishing a maintenance task and restoring the associated integrated function are different evidence judgments."],"answer":2,"explanation":"共享資源會使維護影響跨越單一設備邊界，因此應追蹤相關功能。 課程只建立工程問題，不指定封鎖、隔離、復電或列車營運程序。","explanationEn":"Shared resources let maintenance effects cross device boundaries, so related functions must be traced. The exercise defines engineering questions and specifies no possession, isolation, reenergization or train-operating procedure."}},{"id":"b103-v7-22","sequence":22,"order":4,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-geology","v7-gotthard-construction","v7-gotthard-technical"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v7-21"],"title":"比較缺陷、環境與感測器異常","titleEn":"Compare defects, environment and sensor anomalies","objective":"為維護觀察保留多個候選解釋。","objectiveEn":"Retain multiple explanations for maintenance observations.","instruction":"1. 自設一段滲水及位移紀錄；2. 加入感測器維修與降雨時間；3. 分列可能關係、尚未證實關係及補測需求。","instructionEn":"1. Create synthetic seepage and movement records; 2. add sensor-service and rainfall times; 3. separate possible relations, unproven relations and further evidence.","observation":"同時發生的變化只能提出關聯假說，不能直接證明單一成因。","observationEn":"Coincident changes suggest a relationship but do not prove a single cause.","failure":"降雨後讀數改變便能排除所有設備與基準因素。","failureEn":"A post-rainfall change excludes every equipment and datum explanation.","check":"輸出至少三項候選原因的證據評分表。","checkEn":"Provide an evidence table for at least three candidate causes.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v7-22-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"因果判讀需要時間、空間及獨立證據一致；單一相關不足以診斷。","textEn":"Causal interpretation needs consistent temporal, spatial and independent evidence; correlation alone is insufficient."},{"id":"b103-v7-22-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"維護資料的缺漏與感測器更換必須保留在時間軸上，避免假趨勢。","textEn":"Data gaps and sensor replacements belong on the timeline to avoid false trends."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「比較缺陷、環境與感測器異常」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Compare defects, environment and sensor anomalies”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["同時發生的變化只能提出關聯假說，不能直接證明單一成因。","降雨後讀數改變便能排除所有設備與基準因素。","兩條曲線同時變動足以證明其中一條必然造成另一條。"],"optionsEn":["Coincident changes suggest a relationship but do not prove a single cause.","A post-rainfall change excludes every equipment and datum explanation.","Simultaneous changes prove one curve necessarily causes the other."],"answer":0,"explanation":"因果判讀需要時間、空間及獨立證據一致；單一相關不足以診斷。 維護資料的缺漏與感測器更換必須保留在時間軸上，避免假趨勢。","explanationEn":"Causal interpretation needs consistent temporal, spatial and independent evidence; correlation alone is insufficient. Data gaps and sensor replacements belong on the timeline to avoid false trends."}},{"id":"b103-v7-23","sequence":23,"order":5,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-geology","v7-gotthard-construction","v7-gotthard-technical"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v7-22"],"title":"比較海峽、山岳與都市隧道","titleEn":"Compare strait, mountain and urban tunnels","objective":"找出哥達、英法與雪山隧道可互學的問題。","objectiveEn":"Identify transferable questions among Gotthard, Channel and Hsuehshan tunnels.","instruction":"1. 查各隧道用途與場址；2. 比較水、地質、運輸及連通需求；3. 列出共同的證據管理方法與不可沿用的參數。","instructionEn":"1. Verify each tunnel’s use and setting; 2. compare water, geology, transport and connection requirements; 3. separate shared evidence methods from nontransferable parameters.","observation":"地質更新及介面追溯可互學，但鐵路與公路的營運需求不同。","observationEn":"Geological updating and interface traceability transfer, but rail and road operational requirements differ.","failure":"都是長隧道就可套用同一通風、斷面與行車模型。","failureEn":"All long tunnels can share the same ventilation, section and traffic model.","check":"提交三隧道的相似處與差異表。","checkEn":"Provide a three-tunnel similarity and difference table.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v7-23-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"工程比較要保持系統邊界清楚，不能把隧道長度當成唯一難度指標。","textEn":"Comparisons need clear system boundaries and cannot use length as the sole complexity measure."},{"id":"b103-v7-23-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"延伸研究應從各營運者與業主資料重新建模，而非將本課程假設直接複製。","textEn":"Related research should rebuild from operator and owner evidence rather than copy this course’s assumptions."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「比較海峽、山岳與都市隧道」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Compare strait, mountain and urban tunnels”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["都是長隧道就可套用同一通風、斷面與行車模型。","地質更新及介面追溯可互學，但鐵路與公路的營運需求不同。","公路與鐵路隧道可直接共用全部營運假設。"],"optionsEn":["All long tunnels can share the same ventilation, section and traffic model.","Geological updating and interface traceability transfer, but rail and road operational requirements differ.","Road and railway tunnels can directly reuse every operating assumption."],"answer":1,"explanation":"工程比較要保持系統邊界清楚，不能把隧道長度當成唯一難度指標。 延伸研究應從各營運者與業主資料重新建模，而非將本課程假設直接複製。","explanationEn":"Comparisons need clear system boundaries and cannot use length as the sole complexity measure. Related research should rebuild from operator and owner evidence rather than copy this course’s assumptions."}},{"id":"b103-v7-24","sequence":24,"order":6,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-geology","v7-gotthard-construction","v7-gotthard-technical"],"simulationOnly":true,"estimatedMinutes":25,"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v7-23"],"title":"交付隧道系統學習檔案","titleEn":"Deliver the tunnel-system learning dossier","objective":"把地質到鐵路服務串成可追溯鏈。","objectiveEn":"Connect geology to railway service through a traceable chain.","instruction":"1. 整合路線、地質、狀態及系統圖；2. 每個判讀連接來源與假設；3. 用一項地質變更重新追查下游影響。","instructionEn":"1. Integrate route, geology, state and system diagrams; 2. link each interpretation to sources and assumptions; 3. trace downstream impacts of one ground-model change.","observation":"可追溯檔案能指出證據改變後哪些結論需重驗。","observationEn":"A traceable dossier identifies conclusions requiring recheck after evidence changes.","failure":"所有課程步驟打勾就代表真實隧道具備營運安全認證。","failureEn":"Checking every lesson step certifies an actual tunnel’s operational safety.","check":"繳交四階段索引、未解問題與一次修訂演練。","checkEn":"Submit a four-stage index, unresolved questions and one revision exercise.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v7-24-k1","title":"機理與邊界","titleEn":"Mechanism and boundary","text":"隧道是地盤、結構、設備及營運共同組成的系統，驗證必須跨越專業邊界。","textEn":"A tunnel combines ground, structures, equipment and operations, so verification crosses disciplinary boundaries."},{"id":"b103-v7-24-k2","title":"證據與推論","titleEn":"Evidence and inference","text":"學習完成表示已建立概念與證據組織，不表示具備現地挖掘或營運權限。","textEn":"Completion demonstrates conceptual and evidence organization, not permission for field excavation or operation."}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「交付隧道系統學習檔案」時，哪個判讀有根據？","questionEn":"When reviewing “Deliver the tunnel-system learning dossier”, which interpretation is justified?","options":["所有課程步驟打勾就代表真實隧道具備營運安全認證。","新證據不應改變先前已完成的任何模型結論。","可追溯檔案能指出證據改變後哪些結論需重驗。"],"optionsEn":["Checking every lesson step certifies an actual tunnel’s operational safety.","New evidence should never change a previously completed model conclusion.","A traceable dossier identifies conclusions requiring recheck after evidence changes."],"answer":2,"explanation":"隧道是地盤、結構、設備及營運共同組成的系統，驗證必須跨越專業邊界。 學習完成表示已建立概念與證據組織，不表示具備現地挖掘或營運權限。","explanationEn":"A tunnel combines ground, structures, equipment and operations, so verification crosses disciplinary boundaries. Completion demonstrates conceptual and evidence organization, not permission for field excavation or operation."}}]},{"id":"b103-v14-s1","title":"地層條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Ground conditions, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「基線縱坡與牽引需求」與「覆土應力與洞壁重分配」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Base-alignment grade and traction demand\" and \"Cover stress and wall redistribution\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b103-v14-01","title":"基線縱坡與牽引需求：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Base-alignment grade and traction demand: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v7-24"],"objective":"說明「坡度阻力功率」如何影響哥達基線隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Grade-resistance power” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Gotthard Base Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"哥達基線的低坡度目標必須和重載列車情境一起評估，減少坡度阻力不表示通風氣動與加速功率可忽略。基線鐵路用較小縱坡降低重載列車的重力阻力，但仍有滾動、空氣阻力及加速需求。土建線形和供電容量必須使用同一列車與速度情境，短距陡坡也不能被平均坡度掩蓋；制動方向的能量處理則是另一個需要獨立檢核的工況。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「坡度阻力功率」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Assess Gotthard’s low-gradient purpose with heavy-train scenarios; reduced gravity resistance does not eliminate aerodynamic, acceleration or ventilation demands. A base alignment reduces heavy-train gravity resistance through gentler gradients, but rolling resistance, aerodynamic drag and acceleration remain. Civil geometry and power capacity must use consistent train and speed cases. Short steep sections cannot be hidden in an average gradient, while braking energy in the opposite direction requires its own operating and electrical assessment. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Grade-resistance power” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：列車質量=1.24e+06 kg；縱坡=0.005 無因次；速度=20 m/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: train mass=1.24e+06 kg; grade=0.005 dimensionless; speed=20 m/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「基線隧道坡度很小，所以不必做牽引與制動分析。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A small base-tunnel gradient eliminates the need for traction and braking analysis.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「坡度阻力功率」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Grade-resistance power”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v14-01-k1","title":"基線縱坡與牽引需求","titleEn":"Base-alignment grade and traction demand","text":"哥達基線的低坡度目標必須和重載列車情境一起評估，減少坡度阻力不表示通風氣動與加速功率可忽略。基線鐵路用較小縱坡降低重載列車的重力阻力，但仍有滾動、空氣阻力及加速需求。","textEn":"Assess Gotthard’s low-gradient purpose with heavy-train scenarios; reduced gravity resistance does not eliminate aerodynamic, acceleration or ventilation demands. A base alignment reduces heavy-train gravity resistance through gentler gradients, but rolling resistance, aerodynamic drag and acceleration remain.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b103-v14-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：基線隧道坡度很小，所以不必做牽引與制動分析。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A small base-tunnel gradient eliminates the need for traction and braking analysis. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「基線縱坡與牽引需求」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Base-alignment grade and traction demand\" is correct?","options":["基線隧道坡度很小，所以不必做牽引與制動分析。","哥達基線的低坡度目標必須和重載列車情境一起評估，減少坡度阻力不表示通風氣動與加速功率可忽略。","知道覆土深度就能唯一決定洞壁各方向的應力。"],"optionsEn":["A small base-tunnel gradient eliminates the need for traction and braking analysis.","Assess Gotthard’s low-gradient purpose with heavy-train scenarios.","Cover depth uniquely determines wall stress in every direction."],"answer":1,"explanation":"哥達基線的低坡度目標必須和重載列車情境一起評估，減少坡度阻力不表示通風氣動與加速功率可忽略。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Assess Gotthard’s low-gradient purpose with heavy-train scenarios; reduced gravity resistance does not eliminate aerodynamic, acceleration or ventilation demands. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b103-v14-02","title":"基線縱坡與牽引需求：定量估算","titleEn":"Base-alignment grade and traction demand: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v14-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「坡度阻力功率」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Grade-resistance power” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：列車質量=1.24e+06 kg；縱坡=0.005 無因次；速度=20 m/s。P=mgiv/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=1216.44 kW。僅把縱坡增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為1338.08 kW。邊界：僅坡度阻力，不含滾動、氣動、加速及效率；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: train mass=1.24e+06 kg; grade=0.005 dimensionless; speed=20 m/s. P=mgiv/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=1216.44 kW. Increasing only grade by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 1338.08 kW. Boundary: Grade resistance only, excluding rolling, aerodynamic, acceleration and efficiency losses. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將同一列車在基線與假想山線上的逐段坡度功率比較，再分開制動和牽引需求。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare local grade power for one train on base and hypothetical mountain alignments, separating braking from traction.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v14-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：列車質量=1.24e+06 kg；縱坡=0.005 無因次；速度=20 m/s。P=mgiv/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=1216.44 kW。僅把縱坡增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為1338.08 kW。邊界：僅坡度阻力，不含滾動、氣動、加速及效率；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: train mass=1.24e+06 kg; grade=0.005 dimensionless; speed=20 m/s. P=mgiv/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=1216.44 kW. Increasing only grade by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 1338.08 kW. Boundary: Grade resistance only, excluding rolling, aerodynamic, acceleration and efficiency losses. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b103-v14-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「基線縱坡與牽引需求」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Base-alignment grade and traction demand\", which statement holds?","options":["混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。","增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。","原創教學假設：列車質量=1.24e+06 kg；縱坡=0.005 無因次；速度=20 m/s。"],"optionsEn":["Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure.","Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly.","Original teaching assumptions: train mass=1.24e+06 kg; grade=0.005 dimensionless; speed=20 m/s."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：列車質量=1.24e+06 kg；縱坡=0.005 無因次；速度=20 m/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: train mass=1.24e+06 kg; grade=0.005 dimensionless; speed=20 m/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b103-v14-03","title":"基線縱坡與牽引需求：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Base-alignment grade and traction demand: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v14-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「坡度阻力功率」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Grade-resistance power” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將同一列車在基線與假想山線上的逐段坡度功率比較，再分開制動和牽引需求。以里程高程表逐段計算坡度，對照列車性能曲線和供電模型，另檢核低速牽引及下坡制動，不只比較平均功率。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare local grade power for one train on base and hypothetical mountain alignments, separating braking from traction. Calculate local grades from chainage and elevation, compare with train-performance and power models, and separately check low-speed traction and downhill braking. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「坡度阻力功率」的交付需回答：將同一列車在基線與假想山線上的逐段坡度功率比較，再分開制動和牽引需求。軌頂高程交付前，由土建、軌道、供電和營運共同確認同版線形及列車包絡，變更坡度時同步更新性能與容量計算。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Gotthard Base Tunnel, the grade-resistance power handover must address the following evidence: Compare local grade power for one train on base and hypothetical mountain alignments, separating braking from traction. Civil, track, power and operations teams approve one alignment and train envelope before handover; grade changes update both performance and capacity calculations.","failure":"注意干擾：若只比較最高坡度而忽略長度和速度歷程，節能結論可能偏離整段旅程。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Comparing maximum grade without length and speed history can misstate whole-journey energy benefit. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v14-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將同一列車在基線與假想山線上的逐段坡度功率比較，再分開制動和牽引需求。以里程高程表逐段計算坡度，對照列車性能曲線和供電模型，另檢核低速牽引及下坡制動，不只比較平均功率。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Compare local grade power for one train on base and hypothetical mountain alignments, separating braking from traction. Calculate local grades from chainage and elevation, compare with train-performance and power models, and separately check low-speed traction and downhill braking. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b103-v14-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「坡度阻力功率」的交付需回答：將同一列車在基線與假想山線上的逐段坡度功率比較，再分開制動和牽引需求。軌頂高程交付前，由土建、軌道、供電和營運共同確認同版線形及列車包絡，變更坡度時同步更新性能與容量計算。","textEn":"For Gotthard Base Tunnel, the grade-resistance power handover must address the following evidence: Compare local grade power for one train on base and hypothetical mountain alignments, separating braking from traction. Civil, track, power and operations teams approve one alignment and train envelope before handover; grade changes update both performance and capacity calculations.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「基線縱坡與牽引需求」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Base-alignment grade and traction demand\"?","options":["將同一列車在基線與假想山線上的逐段坡度功率比較，再分開制動和牽引需求。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、開挖序列與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","只要體積風量相同，不同海拔的空氣散熱量一定相同。"],"optionsEn":["Compare local grade power for one train on base and hypothetical mountain alignments, separating braking from traction.","Temperature, water head, excavation sequence and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Equal volumetric airflow provides identical cooling at every altitude."],"answer":0,"explanation":"將同一列車在基線與假想山線上的逐段坡度功率比較，再分開制動和牽引需求。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare local grade power for one train on base and hypothetical mountain alignments, separating braking from traction. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b103-v14-04","title":"基線縱坡與牽引需求：失效診斷","titleEn":"Base-alignment grade and traction demand: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v14-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「坡度阻力功率」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Grade-resistance power” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若只比較最高坡度而忽略長度和速度歷程，節能結論可能偏離整段旅程。平均坡度低卻存在短陡坡時，峰值功率可能超過預估，速度下降又會增加區段占用時間，牽連營運容量。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Comparing maximum grade without length and speed history can misstate whole-journey energy benefit. A short steep grade can exceed power estimates despite a low average, reducing speed and extending block occupation with capacity consequences. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：土建線形和供電容量必須使用同一列車與速度情境，短距陡坡也不能被平均坡度掩蓋；制動方向的能量處理則是另一個需要獨立檢核的工況。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Short steep sections cannot be hidden in an average gradient, while braking energy in the opposite direction requires its own operating and electrical assessment.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「基線隧道坡度很小，所以不必做牽引與制動分析。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A small base-tunnel gradient eliminates the need for traction and braking analysis.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v14-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若只比較最高坡度而忽略長度和速度歷程，節能結論可能偏離整段旅程。平均坡度低卻存在短陡坡時，峰值功率可能超過預估，速度下降又會增加區段占用時間，牽連營運容量。","textEn":"Comparing maximum grade without length and speed history can misstate whole-journey energy benefit. A short steep grade can exceed power estimates despite a low average, reducing speed and extending block occupation with capacity consequences.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b103-v14-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「基線縱坡與牽引需求」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Base-alignment grade and traction demand\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","若只比較最高坡度而忽略長度和速度歷程，節能結論可能偏離整段旅程。","知道覆土深度就能唯一決定洞壁各方向的應力。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Comparing maximum grade without length and speed history can misstate whole-journey energy benefit.","Cover depth uniquely determines wall stress in every direction."],"answer":1,"explanation":"若只比較最高坡度而忽略長度和速度歷程，節能結論可能偏離整段旅程。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Comparing maximum grade without length and speed history can misstate whole-journey energy benefit. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b103-v14-05","title":"覆土應力與洞壁重分配：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Cover stress and wall redistribution: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v14-04"],"objective":"說明「洞壁切向應力」如何影響哥達基線隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Tangential wall stress” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Gotthard Base Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"哥達深覆土的教學模型先分開遠場應力與洞壁集中，研究同一覆土下不同水平應力比對破壞方向的影響。開挖使岩體洞壁失去徑向拘束，遠場荷載轉移到周圍岩體，局部切向應力可能升高。圓孔彈性解可辨識量級，但節理、非圓斷面、塑性區與原位應力比會改變峰值位置，不能只用覆土重量推定全部三維應力。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「洞壁切向應力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Separate remote stress from wall concentration in deep cover and examine how different horizontal stress ratios change damage orientation at the same depth. Excavation removes radial confinement at the wall and transfers load through the surrounding rock, potentially raising local tangential stress. An elastic circular-hole solution identifies scale, but joints, noncircular geometry, yielding and the in-situ stress ratio alter the peak location. Cover weight alone cannot establish the complete three-dimensional stress state or support demand. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Tangential wall stress” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：覆土深度=560 m；岩體單位重=26 kN/m³。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: cover=560 m; rock unit weight=26 kN/m³. σθ,max=3γH/1000=43.68 MPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「知道覆土深度就能唯一決定洞壁各方向的應力。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Cover depth uniquely determines wall stress in every direction.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「洞壁切向應力」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Tangential wall stress”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v14-05-k1","title":"覆土應力與洞壁重分配","titleEn":"Cover stress and wall redistribution","text":"哥達深覆土的教學模型先分開遠場應力與洞壁集中，研究同一覆土下不同水平應力比對破壞方向的影響。開挖使岩體洞壁失去徑向拘束，遠場荷載轉移到周圍岩體，局部切向應力可能升高。","textEn":"Separate remote stress from wall concentration in deep cover and examine how different horizontal stress ratios change damage orientation at the same depth. Excavation removes radial confinement at the wall and transfers load through the surrounding rock, potentially raising local tangential stress.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b103-v14-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：知道覆土深度就能唯一決定洞壁各方向的應力。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Cover depth uniquely determines wall stress in every direction. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「覆土應力與洞壁重分配」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Cover stress and wall redistribution\" is correct?","options":["知道覆土深度就能唯一決定洞壁各方向的應力。","支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。","哥達深覆土的教學模型先分開遠場應力與洞壁集中，研究同一覆土下不同水平應力比對破壞方向的影響。"],"optionsEn":["Cover depth uniquely determines wall stress in every direction.","Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem.","Separate remote stress from wall concentration in deep cover and examine how different horizontal stress ratios change damage orientation at the same depth."],"answer":2,"explanation":"哥達深覆土的教學模型先分開遠場應力與洞壁集中，研究同一覆土下不同水平應力比對破壞方向的影響。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Separate remote stress from wall concentration in deep cover and examine how different horizontal stress ratios change damage orientation at the same depth. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b103-v14-06","title":"覆土應力與洞壁重分配：定量估算","titleEn":"Cover stress and wall redistribution: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v14-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「洞壁切向應力」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Tangential wall stress” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：覆土深度=560 m；岩體單位重=26 kN/m³。σθ,max=3γH/1000=43.68 MPa。僅把覆土深度增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為48.048 MPa。邊界：無支承彈性圓孔，僅垂直遠場壓縮且水平遠場應力為零時，側壁最大環向壓應力；不是任意位置應力或完整三維原位解；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: cover=560 m; rock unit weight=26 kN/m³. σθ,max=3γH/1000=43.68 MPa. Increasing only cover by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 48.048 MPa. Boundary: Maximum tangential compression at the sidewalls of an unsupported elastic circular hole under vertical uniaxial remote loading with zero horizontal remote stress; not stress at any point or the complete three-dimensional in-situ state. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：把洞壁破壞方位與原位應力及節理方向比對，測試各模型是否預測同一高需求區。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare wall-damage orientation with stress and joints, testing whether alternative models predict the same critical zone.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v14-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：覆土深度=560 m；岩體單位重=26 kN/m³。σθ,max=3γH/1000=43.68 MPa。僅把覆土深度增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為48.048 MPa。邊界：無支承彈性圓孔，僅垂直遠場壓縮且水平遠場應力為零時，側壁最大環向壓應力；不是任意位置應力或完整三維原位解；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: cover=560 m; rock unit weight=26 kN/m³. σθ,max=3γH/1000=43.68 MPa. Increasing only cover by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 48.048 MPa. Boundary: Maximum tangential compression at the sidewalls of an unsupported elastic circular hole under vertical uniaxial remote loading with zero horizontal remote stress; not stress at any point or the complete three-dimensional in-situ state. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b103-v14-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「覆土應力與洞壁重分配」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Cover stress and wall redistribution\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：覆土深度=560 m；岩體單位重=26 kN/m³。","刀盤瞬間轉得更快就保證全工程平均進尺更高。","兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: cover=560 m; rock unit weight=26 kN/m³. σθ,max=3γH/1000=43.68 MPa.","A faster instantaneous cutterhead speed guarantees higher project-average advance.","Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：覆土深度=560 m；岩體單位重=26 kN/m³。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: cover=560 m; rock unit weight=26 kN/m³. σθ,max=3γH/1000=43.68 MPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b103-v14-07","title":"覆土應力與洞壁重分配：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Cover stress and wall redistribution: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v14-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「洞壁切向應力」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Tangential wall stress” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"把洞壁破壞方位與原位應力及節理方向比對，測試各模型是否預測同一高需求區。將原位應力量測、岩石試驗及洞壁破壞方位相互比較，再用多點伸長計檢查變形是否與所假設應力方向一致。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare wall-damage orientation with stress and joints, testing whether alternative models predict the same critical zone. Compare in-situ stress measurements, rock tests and wall-damage orientation, then use multipoint extensometers to test consistency with the assumed stress directions. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「洞壁切向應力」的交付需回答：把洞壁破壞方位與原位應力及節理方向比對，測試各模型是否預測同一高需求區。保留應力模型的座標、邊界和材料假設，量測與預測不符時先核對代表性，再由岩力設計者選擇非線性或節理模型。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Gotthard Base Tunnel, the tangential wall stress handover must address the following evidence: Compare wall-damage orientation with stress and joints, testing whether alternative models predict the same critical zone. Record stress-model coordinates, boundaries and material assumptions; when observations disagree, check representativeness before the rock designer selects nonlinear or jointed models.","failure":"注意干擾：以覆土唯一決定應力會錯估側壁或拱頂哪處先受損，進而誤置觀測點。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using cover alone can misidentify whether walls or crown govern and place monitoring at the wrong location. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v14-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"把洞壁破壞方位與原位應力及節理方向比對，測試各模型是否預測同一高需求區。將原位應力量測、岩石試驗及洞壁破壞方位相互比較，再用多點伸長計檢查變形是否與所假設應力方向一致。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Compare wall-damage orientation with stress and joints, testing whether alternative models predict the same critical zone. Compare in-situ stress measurements, rock tests and wall-damage orientation, then use multipoint extensometers to test consistency with the assumed stress directions. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b103-v14-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「洞壁切向應力」的交付需回答：把洞壁破壞方位與原位應力及節理方向比對，測試各模型是否預測同一高需求區。保留應力模型的座標、邊界和材料假設，量測與預測不符時先核對代表性，再由岩力設計者選擇非線性或節理模型。","textEn":"For Gotthard Base Tunnel, the tangential wall stress handover must address the following evidence: Compare wall-damage orientation with stress and joints, testing whether alternative models predict the same critical zone. Record stress-model coordinates, boundaries and material assumptions; when observations disagree, check representativeness before the rock designer selects nonlinear or jointed models.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「覆土應力與洞壁重分配」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Cover stress and wall redistribution\"?","options":["沿用另一條隧道或另一處地層的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","把洞壁破壞方位與原位應力及節理方向比對，測試各模型是否預測同一高需求區。","動壓公式算出的數值就是長鐵路隧道完整壓力波。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another tunnel or ground formation counts as verifying this structure.","Compare wall-damage orientation with stress and joints, testing whether alternative models predict the same critical zone.","A dynamic-pressure calculation is the complete pressure-wave prediction for a long rail tunnel."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把洞壁破壞方位與原位應力及節理方向比對，測試各模型是否預測同一高需求區。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare wall-damage orientation with stress and joints, testing whether alternative models predict the same critical zone. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b103-v14-08","title":"覆土應力與洞壁重分配：失效診斷","titleEn":"Cover stress and wall redistribution: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v14-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「洞壁切向應力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Tangential wall stress” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"以覆土唯一決定應力會錯估側壁或拱頂哪處先受損，進而誤置觀測點。把彈性峰值直接當岩體強度可能誤判支護需求；相反地忽略剝落或擠壓也會讓局部破壞逐步侵入淨空。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using cover alone can misidentify whether walls or crown govern and place monitoring at the wrong location. Equating an elastic peak with rock-mass strength misjudges support demand; overlooking spalling or squeezing lets damage progressively consume clearance. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：圓孔彈性解可辨識量級，但節理、非圓斷面、塑性區與原位應力比會改變峰值位置，不能只用覆土重量推定全部三維應力。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Cover weight alone cannot establish the complete three-dimensional stress state or support demand.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「知道覆土深度就能唯一決定洞壁各方向的應力。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Cover depth uniquely determines wall stress in every direction.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v14-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"以覆土唯一決定應力會錯估側壁或拱頂哪處先受損，進而誤置觀測點。把彈性峰值直接當岩體強度可能誤判支護需求；相反地忽略剝落或擠壓也會讓局部破壞逐步侵入淨空。","textEn":"Using cover alone can misidentify whether walls or crown govern and place monitoring at the wrong location. Equating an elastic peak with rock-mass strength misjudges support demand; overlooking spalling or squeezing lets damage progressively consume clearance.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b103-v14-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「覆土應力與洞壁重分配」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Cover stress and wall redistribution\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。","以覆土唯一決定應力會錯估側壁或拱頂哪處先受損，進而誤置觀測點。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem.","Using cover alone can misidentify whether walls or crown govern and place monitoring at the wrong location."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以覆土唯一決定應力會錯估側壁或拱頂哪處先受損，進而誤置觀測點。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using cover alone can misidentify whether walls or crown govern and place monitoring at the wrong location. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":5},{"id":"b103-v14-s2","title":"機制、材料與定量設計","titleEn":"Mechanisms, materials and quantitative design","description":"本階段聚焦「支護啟動與變形容量」與「環向受力與接縫柔度」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Support activation and deformation capacity\" and \"Ring force and joint flexibility\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b103-v14-09","title":"支護啟動與變形容量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Support activation and deformation capacity: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v14-08"],"objective":"說明「支護安裝時點」如何影響哥達基線隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Support activation time” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Gotthard Base Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"哥達多地質區段的支護不能只以最終厚度比較，需把安裝距離和可容許變形納入，理解何時剛性過高反而增加局部需求。支護荷載由開挖釋放量和支護啟動時間共同決定，越早安裝不一定讓構件受力越小。地盤反力與支護曲線必須連同掌子面距離及封閉順序理解；擠壓性地層還需保留變形容量，不能只追求高剛度與高材料強度。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「支護安裝時點」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Compare support across ground domains using activation distance and deformation allowance, not final thickness alone, and identify when excess stiffness increases local demand. Support load depends on stress release and activation time, so earlier installation does not necessarily reduce member forces. Interpret ground-reaction and support curves together with distance from the face and closure sequence. Squeezing ground also needs deformation capacity; high stiffness and material strength alone do not guarantee a compatible support response. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Support activation time” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：局部剛度=32 kN/mm；位移=7 mm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: local stiffness=32 kN/mm; movement=7 mm.","failure":"常見誤解：「支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「支護安裝時點」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Support activation time”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v14-09-k1","title":"支護啟動與變形容量","titleEn":"Support activation and deformation capacity","text":"哥達多地質區段的支護不能只以最終厚度比較，需把安裝距離和可容許變形納入，理解何時剛性過高反而增加局部需求。支護荷載由開挖釋放量和支護啟動時間共同決定，越早安裝不一定讓構件受力越小。","textEn":"Compare support across ground domains using activation distance and deformation allowance, not final thickness alone, and identify when excess stiffness increases local demand. Support load depends on stress release and activation time, so earlier installation does not necessarily reduce member forces.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b103-v14-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「支護啟動與變形容量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Support activation and deformation capacity\" is correct?","options":["哥達多地質區段的支護不能只以最終厚度比較，需把安裝距離和可容許變形納入，理解何時剛性過高反而增加局部需求。","支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。","混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。"],"optionsEn":["Compare support across ground domains using activation distance and deformation allowance, not final thickness alone, and identify when excess stiffness increases local demand.","Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem.","Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure."],"answer":0,"explanation":"哥達多地質區段的支護不能只以最終厚度比較，需把安裝距離和可容許變形納入，理解何時剛性過高反而增加局部需求。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Compare support across ground domains using activation distance and deformation allowance, not final thickness alone, and identify when excess stiffness increases local demand. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b103-v14-10","title":"支護啟動與變形容量：定量估算","titleEn":"Support activation and deformation capacity: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v14-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「支護安裝時點」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Support activation time” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：局部剛度=32 kN/mm；位移=7 mm。F=ku=224 kN。僅把位移增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為246.4 kN。邊界：線性局部彈簧，不含屈服或時間效應；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: local stiffness=32 kN/mm; movement=7 mm. F=ku=224 kN. Increasing only movement by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 246.4 kN. Boundary: Local linear spring without yielding or time effects. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：按掌子面距離重排收斂與荷重資料，檢查不同區段能否用同一支護曲線解釋。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Replot convergence and load against face distance, testing whether one support curve explains different sections.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v14-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：局部剛度=32 kN/mm；位移=7 mm。F=ku=224 kN。僅把位移增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為246.4 kN。邊界：線性局部彈簧，不含屈服或時間效應；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: local stiffness=32 kN/mm; movement=7 mm. F=ku=224 kN. Increasing only movement by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 246.4 kN. Boundary: Local linear spring without yielding or time effects. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b103-v14-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「支護啟動與變形容量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Support activation and deformation capacity\", which statement holds?","options":["增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。","原創教學假設：局部剛度=32 kN/mm；位移=7 mm。","只要體積風量相同，不同海拔的空氣散熱量一定相同。"],"optionsEn":["Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly.","Original teaching assumptions: local stiffness=32 kN/mm; movement=7 mm.","Equal volumetric airflow provides identical cooling at every altitude."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：局部剛度=32 kN/mm；位移=7 mm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: local stiffness=32 kN/mm; movement=7 mm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b103-v14-11","title":"支護啟動與變形容量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Support activation and deformation capacity: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v14-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「支護安裝時點」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Support activation time” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"按掌子面距離重排收斂與荷重資料，檢查不同區段能否用同一支護曲線解釋。同步記錄收斂、支護荷重與安裝里程，比較同一地質分區內的速率及荷載，不將不同開挖齡期讀值直接混合。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Replot convergence and load against face distance, testing whether one support curve explains different sections. Synchronise convergence, support loads and installation chainage; compare rates and loads within one ground domain without mixing readings at different excavation ages. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「支護安裝時點」的交付需回答：按掌子面距離重排收斂與荷重資料，檢查不同區段能否用同一支護曲線解釋。把安裝時間和量測資料一起交付支護設計者，任何級別變更都需地質及位移證據，不能憑單一瞬間讀值自行改支護。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Gotthard Base Tunnel, the support activation time handover must address the following evidence: Replot convergence and load against face distance, testing whether one support curve explains different sections. Submit installation times with measurements to the support designer; class changes need both ground and movement evidence, not an isolated instantaneous reading.","failure":"注意干擾：把不同安裝時點的讀值混合會誤判材料剛度，可能把施工順序問題當材料缺陷。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Mixing activation times biases inferred stiffness and can misclassify a sequence problem as a material defect. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v14-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"按掌子面距離重排收斂與荷重資料，檢查不同區段能否用同一支護曲線解釋。同步記錄收斂、支護荷重與安裝里程，比較同一地質分區內的速率及荷載，不將不同開挖齡期讀值直接混合。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Replot convergence and load against face distance, testing whether one support curve explains different sections. Synchronise convergence, support loads and installation chainage; compare rates and loads within one ground domain without mixing readings at different excavation ages. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b103-v14-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「支護安裝時點」的交付需回答：按掌子面距離重排收斂與荷重資料，檢查不同區段能否用同一支護曲線解釋。把安裝時間和量測資料一起交付支護設計者，任何級別變更都需地質及位移證據，不能憑單一瞬間讀值自行改支護。","textEn":"For Gotthard Base Tunnel, the support activation time handover must address the following evidence: Replot convergence and load against face distance, testing whether one support curve explains different sections. Submit installation times with measurements to the support designer; class changes need both ground and movement evidence, not an isolated instantaneous reading.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「支護啟動與變形容量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Support activation and deformation capacity\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。","按掌子面距離重排收斂與荷重資料，檢查不同區段能否用同一支護曲線解釋。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.","Replot convergence and load against face distance, testing whether one support curve explains different sections."],"answer":2,"explanation":"按掌子面距離重排收斂與荷重資料，檢查不同區段能否用同一支護曲線解釋。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Replot convergence and load against face distance, testing whether one support curve explains different sections. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b103-v14-12","title":"支護啟動與變形容量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Support activation and deformation capacity: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v14-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「支護安裝時點」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Support activation time” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把不同安裝時點的讀值混合會誤判材料剛度，可能把施工順序問題當材料缺陷。過晚封閉會讓不可回復變形增加，過硬且行程不足的支護也可能脆裂，兩者都可能表現為裂縫而需不同處理。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Mixing activation times biases inferred stiffness and can misclassify a sequence problem as a material defect. Late closure increases irreversible movement, while excessively stiff support with little travel can fail brittly; both produce cracks but require different diagnoses. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：地盤反力與支護曲線必須連同掌子面距離及封閉順序理解；擠壓性地層還需保留變形容量，不能只追求高剛度與高材料強度。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Squeezing ground also needs deformation capacity; high stiffness and material strength alone do not guarantee a compatible support response.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v14-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把不同安裝時點的讀值混合會誤判材料剛度，可能把施工順序問題當材料缺陷。過晚封閉會讓不可回復變形增加，過硬且行程不足的支護也可能脆裂，兩者都可能表現為裂縫而需不同處理。","textEn":"Mixing activation times biases inferred stiffness and can misclassify a sequence problem as a material defect. Late closure increases irreversible movement, while excessively stiff support with little travel can fail brittly; both produce cracks but require different diagnoses.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b103-v14-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「支護啟動與變形容量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Support activation and deformation capacity\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["把不同安裝時點的讀值混合會誤判材料剛度，可能把施工順序問題當材料缺陷。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。"],"optionsEn":["Mixing activation times biases inferred stiffness and can misclassify a sequence problem as a material defect.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure."],"answer":0,"explanation":"把不同安裝時點的讀值混合會誤判材料剛度，可能把施工順序問題當材料缺陷。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Mixing activation times biases inferred stiffness and can misclassify a sequence problem as a material defect. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b103-v14-13","title":"環向受力與接縫柔度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Ring force and joint flexibility: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v14-12"],"objective":"說明「襯砌環向壓縮」如何影響哥達基線隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Lining hoop compression” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Gotthard Base Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"長基線隧道的襯砌須接收地盤、水壓及施工頂推等不同作用，哥達情境比較均勻外壓估算與接頭局部彎曲，避免只用厚度判斷可靠性。圓形襯砌對均勻外壓可主要以環向壓縮抵抗，但接頭轉動、偏壓與背填空隙會引起彎矩。薄環膜應力只說明其中一條受力路徑；脫模、運輸、頂推及永久狀態的荷載不同，環片局部接觸與止水條件必須另外檢核。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「襯砌環向壓縮」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"For the long base-tunnel context, compare uniform-pressure lining estimates with local joint bending under ground, water and construction actions rather than judging reliability by thickness alone. A circular lining resists uniform external pressure largely through hoop compression, but joint rotation, uneven load and backfill voids generate bending. Thin-ring membrane stress describes only one load path. Demoulding, transport, jacking and permanent states impose different actions, requiring separate checks of local segment contact and sealing rather than one permanent-load calculation. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Lining hoop compression” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：均勻外壓=0.34 MPa；半徑=3.3 m；厚度=0.35 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: uniform external pressure=0.34 MPa; radius=3.3 m; thickness=0.35 m. σθ=pr/t=3.20571 MPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「襯砌環向壓縮」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Lining hoop compression”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v14-13-k1","title":"環向受力與接縫柔度","titleEn":"Ring force and joint flexibility","text":"長基線隧道的襯砌須接收地盤、水壓及施工頂推等不同作用，哥達情境比較均勻外壓估算與接頭局部彎曲，避免只用厚度判斷可靠性。圓形襯砌對均勻外壓可主要以環向壓縮抵抗，但接頭轉動、偏壓與背填空隙會引起彎矩。","textEn":"For the long base-tunnel context, compare uniform-pressure lining estimates with local joint bending under ground, water and construction actions rather than judging reliability by thickness alone. A circular lining resists uniform external pressure largely through hoop compression, but joint rotation, uneven load and backfill voids generate bending.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b103-v14-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「環向受力與接縫柔度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Ring force and joint flexibility\" is correct?","options":["混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。","長基線隧道的襯砌須接收地盤、水壓及施工頂推等不同作用，哥達情境比較均勻外壓估算與接頭局部彎曲，避免只用厚度判斷可靠性。","刀盤瞬間轉得更快就保證全工程平均進尺更高。"],"optionsEn":["Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure.","For the long base-tunnel context, compare uniform-pressure lining estimates with local joint bending under ground, water and construction actions rather than judging reliability by thickness alone.","A faster instantaneous cutterhead speed guarantees higher project-average advance."],"answer":1,"explanation":"長基線隧道的襯砌須接收地盤、水壓及施工頂推等不同作用，哥達情境比較均勻外壓估算與接頭局部彎曲，避免只用厚度判斷可靠性。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"For the long base-tunnel context, compare uniform-pressure lining estimates with local joint bending under ground, water and construction actions rather than judging reliability by thickness alone. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b103-v14-14","title":"環向受力與接縫柔度：定量估算","titleEn":"Ring force and joint flexibility: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v14-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「襯砌環向壓縮」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Lining hoop compression” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：均勻外壓=0.34 MPa；半徑=3.3 m；厚度=0.35 m。σθ=pr/t=3.20571 MPa。僅把均勻外壓增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為3.52629 MPa。邊界：薄圓環膜應力，不是接縫、偏壓或矩形框架解；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: uniform external pressure=0.34 MPa; radius=3.3 m; thickness=0.35 m. σθ=pr/t=3.20571 MPa. Increasing only uniform external pressure by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 3.52629 MPa. Boundary: Thin circular-ring membrane stress, not a joint, uneven-load or rectangular-frame solution. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：量測環向變形及接縫開口，將背填和水頭回升階段分開，再對照接頭剛度敏感度。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure ring distortion and joint gaps by grouting and head-recovery stage, comparing joint-stiffness sensitivity.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v14-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：均勻外壓=0.34 MPa；半徑=3.3 m；厚度=0.35 m。σθ=pr/t=3.20571 MPa。僅把均勻外壓增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為3.52629 MPa。邊界：薄圓環膜應力，不是接縫、偏壓或矩形框架解；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: uniform external pressure=0.34 MPa; radius=3.3 m; thickness=0.35 m. σθ=pr/t=3.20571 MPa. Increasing only uniform external pressure by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 3.52629 MPa. Boundary: Thin circular-ring membrane stress, not a joint, uneven-load or rectangular-frame solution. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b103-v14-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「環向受力與接縫柔度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Ring force and joint flexibility\", which statement holds?","options":["兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。","動壓公式算出的數值就是長鐵路隧道完整壓力波。","原創教學假設：均勻外壓=0.34 MPa；半徑=3.3 m；厚度=0.35 m。"],"optionsEn":["Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error.","A dynamic-pressure calculation is the complete pressure-wave prediction for a long rail tunnel.","Original teaching assumptions: uniform external pressure=0.34 MPa; radius=3.3 m; thickness=0.35 m. σθ=pr/t=3.20571 MPa."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：均勻外壓=0.34 MPa；半徑=3.3 m；厚度=0.35 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: uniform external pressure=0.34 MPa; radius=3.3 m; thickness=0.35 m. σθ=pr/t=3.20571 MPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b103-v14-15","title":"環向受力與接縫柔度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Ring force and joint flexibility: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v14-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「襯砌環向壓縮」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Lining hoop compression” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"量測環向變形及接縫開口，將背填和水頭回升階段分開，再對照接頭剛度敏感度。將環形變形、接縫張開與應變和含接頭彈簧的模型比較，分開安裝後、背填後及水頭回升後的基準。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure ring distortion and joint gaps by grouting and head-recovery stage, comparing joint-stiffness sensitivity. Compare ring distortion, joint opening and strain with a joint-spring model, separating baselines after installation, grouting and head recovery. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「襯砌環向壓縮」的交付需回答：量測環向變形及接縫開口，將背填和水頭回升階段分開，再對照接頭剛度敏感度。設計圖應分開標註各施工階段、接頭剛度及背填條件，構件驗收同時核對幾何、材料批次與止水試驗適用包絡。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Gotthard Base Tunnel, the lining hoop compression handover must address the following evidence: Measure ring distortion and joint gaps by grouting and head-recovery stage, comparing joint-stiffness sensitivity. Drawings distinguish stages, joint stiffness and backfill conditions; component acceptance reconciles geometry, material batches and the applicable sealing-test envelope.","failure":"注意干擾：相同平均應變可能掩蓋一處接縫轉動集中，局部防水需求會比整環平均更不利。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Identical mean strain can hide concentrated rotation at one joint with worse local sealing demand. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v14-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"量測環向變形及接縫開口，將背填和水頭回升階段分開，再對照接頭剛度敏感度。將環形變形、接縫張開與應變和含接頭彈簧的模型比較，分開安裝後、背填後及水頭回升後的基準。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Measure ring distortion and joint gaps by grouting and head-recovery stage, comparing joint-stiffness sensitivity. Compare ring distortion, joint opening and strain with a joint-spring model, separating baselines after installation, grouting and head recovery. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b103-v14-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「襯砌環向壓縮」的交付需回答：量測環向變形及接縫開口，將背填和水頭回升階段分開，再對照接頭剛度敏感度。設計圖應分開標註各施工階段、接頭剛度及背填條件，構件驗收同時核對幾何、材料批次與止水試驗適用包絡。","textEn":"For Gotthard Base Tunnel, the lining hoop compression handover must address the following evidence: Measure ring distortion and joint gaps by grouting and head-recovery stage, comparing joint-stiffness sensitivity. Drawings distinguish stages, joint stiffness and backfill conditions; component acceptance reconciles geometry, material batches and the applicable sealing-test envelope.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「環向受力與接縫柔度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Ring force and joint flexibility\"?","options":["量測環向變形及接縫開口，將背填和水頭回升階段分開，再對照接頭剛度敏感度。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","基線隧道坡度很小，所以不必做牽引與制動分析。"],"optionsEn":["Measure ring distortion and joint gaps by grouting and head-recovery stage, comparing joint-stiffness sensitivity.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","A small base-tunnel gradient eliminates the need for traction and braking analysis."],"answer":0,"explanation":"量測環向變形及接縫開口，將背填和水頭回升階段分開，再對照接頭剛度敏感度。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure ring distortion and joint gaps by grouting and head-recovery stage, comparing joint-stiffness sensitivity. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b103-v14-16","title":"環向受力與接縫柔度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Ring force and joint flexibility: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v14-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「襯砌環向壓縮」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Lining hoop compression” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"相同平均應變可能掩蓋一處接縫轉動集中，局部防水需求會比整環平均更不利。局部脫空增加環片彎曲，裂縫未必代表混凝土平均強度不足；忽略接縫接觸會把補強方向導向錯誤位置。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Identical mean strain can hide concentrated rotation at one joint with worse local sealing demand. Local voids increase bending, so cracks need not indicate inadequate mean concrete strength; neglecting joint contact can misdirect strengthening. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：薄環膜應力只說明其中一條受力路徑；脫模、運輸、頂推及永久狀態的荷載不同，環片局部接觸與止水條件必須另外檢核。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Demoulding, transport, jacking and permanent states impose different actions, requiring separate checks of local segment contact and sealing rather than one permanent-load calculation.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v14-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"相同平均應變可能掩蓋一處接縫轉動集中，局部防水需求會比整環平均更不利。局部脫空增加環片彎曲，裂縫未必代表混凝土平均強度不足；忽略接縫接觸會把補強方向導向錯誤位置。","textEn":"Identical mean strain can hide concentrated rotation at one joint with worse local sealing demand. Local voids increase bending, so cracks need not indicate inadequate mean concrete strength; neglecting joint contact can misdirect strengthening.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b103-v14-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「環向受力與接縫柔度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Ring force and joint flexibility\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","相同平均應變可能掩蓋一處接縫轉動集中，局部防水需求會比整環平均更不利。","刀盤瞬間轉得更快就保證全工程平均進尺更高。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Identical mean strain can hide concentrated rotation at one joint with worse local sealing demand.","A faster instantaneous cutterhead speed guarantees higher project-average advance."],"answer":1,"explanation":"相同平均應變可能掩蓋一處接縫轉動集中，局部防水需求會比整環平均更不利。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Identical mean strain can hide concentrated rotation at one joint with worse local sealing demand. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":6},{"id":"b103-v14-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「掘進利用率與設備停時」與「共享通道與運輸瓶頸」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime\" and \"Shared access and transport bottlenecks\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b103-v14-17","title":"掘進利用率與設備停時：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v14-16"],"objective":"說明「有效掘進利用率」如何影響哥達基線隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Effective boring utilisation” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Gotthard Base Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"哥達施工循環可用來分離切削速率與多工作面的有效利用率，並追問刀具維修時間是否隨地質而改變，不能用最佳單班外推整段工期。TBM瞬時貫入率只描述刀盤切削的一段時間，拼裝、換刀、出渣與維修決定每天真正進尺。岩石強度與磨蝕性對刀具的影響不同，混合掌子面又產生不對稱作用；比較機器績效須按地質分區和停時原因分類，不能只排序最高進尺。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「有效掘進利用率」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Separate cutting rate from multi-heading utilisation and test whether cutter maintenance changes with geology; a best shift cannot be extrapolated to the whole drive. Instantaneous penetration describes only active cutting; erection, cutter changes, muck handling and repairs determine daily advance. Strength and abrasivity affect cutters differently, while mixed faces impose asymmetric loading. Compare performance by ground domain and downtime cause, because the highest short-duration penetration rate can coexist with poor daily production and increased maintenance demand. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Effective boring utilisation” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：切削速率=1.56 m/h；有效利用率=0.31 無因次。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: active penetration=1.56 m/h; utilisation=0.31 dimensionless.","failure":"常見誤解：「刀盤瞬間轉得更快就保證全工程平均進尺更高。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A faster instantaneous cutterhead speed guarantees higher project-average advance.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「有效掘進利用率」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Effective boring utilisation”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v14-17-k1","title":"掘進利用率與設備停時","titleEn":"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime","text":"哥達施工循環可用來分離切削速率與多工作面的有效利用率，並追問刀具維修時間是否隨地質而改變，不能用最佳單班外推整段工期。TBM瞬時貫入率只描述刀盤切削的一段時間，拼裝、換刀、出渣與維修決定每天真正進尺。","textEn":"Separate cutting rate from multi-heading utilisation and test whether cutter maintenance changes with geology; a best shift cannot be extrapolated to the whole drive. Instantaneous penetration describes only active cutting; erection, cutter changes, muck handling and repairs determine daily advance.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b103-v14-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：刀盤瞬間轉得更快就保證全工程平均進尺更高。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A faster instantaneous cutterhead speed guarantees higher project-average advance. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「掘進利用率與設備停時」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime\" is correct?","options":["刀盤瞬間轉得更快就保證全工程平均進尺更高。","增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。","哥達施工循環可用來分離切削速率與多工作面的有效利用率，並追問刀具維修時間是否隨地質而改變，不能用最佳單班外推整段工期。"],"optionsEn":["A faster instantaneous cutterhead speed guarantees higher project-average advance.","Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly.","Separate cutting rate from multi-heading utilisation and test whether cutter maintenance changes with geology."],"answer":2,"explanation":"哥達施工循環可用來分離切削速率與多工作面的有效利用率，並追問刀具維修時間是否隨地質而改變，不能用最佳單班外推整段工期。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Separate cutting rate from multi-heading utilisation and test whether cutter maintenance changes with geology; a best shift cannot be extrapolated to the whole drive. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":41},{"id":"b103-v14-18","title":"掘進利用率與設備停時：定量估算","titleEn":"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v14-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「有效掘進利用率」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Effective boring utilisation” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：切削速率=1.56 m/h；有效利用率=0.31 無因次。D=24vu=11.6064 m/day。僅把有效利用率增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為12.767 m/day。邊界：平均循環模型，未表示地質轉換及停機分布；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: active penetration=1.56 m/h; utilisation=0.31 dimensionless. D=24vu=11.6064 m/day. Increasing only utilisation by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 12.767 m/day. Boundary: Mean-cycle model without ground transitions or downtime distribution. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以完整停時分類配對地質及刀具檢查，另用班次時間閉合檢查有無重複計時。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Pair downtime classes with geology and cutter inspections, closing shift time to detect double-counting.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v14-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：切削速率=1.56 m/h；有效利用率=0.31 無因次。D=24vu=11.6064 m/day。僅把有效利用率增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為12.767 m/day。邊界：平均循環模型，未表示地質轉換及停機分布；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: active penetration=1.56 m/h; utilisation=0.31 dimensionless. D=24vu=11.6064 m/day. Increasing only utilisation by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 12.767 m/day. Boundary: Mean-cycle model without ground transitions or downtime distribution. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b103-v14-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「掘進利用率與設備停時」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：切削速率=1.56 m/h；有效利用率=0.31 無因次。","只要體積風量相同，不同海拔的空氣散熱量一定相同。","全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: active penetration=1.56 m/h; utilisation=0.31 dimensionless.","Equal volumetric airflow provides identical cooling at every altitude.","Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：切削速率=1.56 m/h；有效利用率=0.31 無因次。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: active penetration=1.56 m/h; utilisation=0.31 dimensionless. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":42},{"id":"b103-v14-19","title":"掘進利用率與設備停時：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v14-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「有效掘進利用率」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Effective boring utilisation” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以完整停時分類配對地質及刀具檢查，另用班次時間閉合檢查有無重複計時。由時間戳分離切削、拼裝與故障，將刀具位置、磨耗量及推力扭矩對齊里程，檢查停時是否集中在特定地層。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Pair downtime classes with geology and cutter inspections, closing shift time to detect double-counting. Separate cutting, erection and faults by timestamp; align cutter position, wear, thrust and torque with chainage and test clustering by ground type. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「有效掘進利用率」的交付需回答：以完整停時分類配對地質及刀具檢查，另用班次時間閉合檢查有無重複計時。停機紀錄使用可追溯原因碼，把地質變化與設備故障分開統計，參數調整只能在設備和施工團隊核准程序內進行。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Gotthard Base Tunnel, the effective boring utilisation handover must address the following evidence: Pair downtime classes with geology and cutter inspections, closing shift time to detect double-counting. Use traceable downtime codes, separating geological change from equipment faults; parameter changes stay within procedures approved by equipment and construction teams.","failure":"注意干擾：把換刀和出渣重疊時間加兩次會低估利用率，錯誤地支持增購機械的決策。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Double-counting overlapping cutter and spoil delays understates utilisation and can falsely justify more machinery. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v14-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以完整停時分類配對地質及刀具檢查，另用班次時間閉合檢查有無重複計時。由時間戳分離切削、拼裝與故障，將刀具位置、磨耗量及推力扭矩對齊里程，檢查停時是否集中在特定地層。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Pair downtime classes with geology and cutter inspections, closing shift time to detect double-counting. Separate cutting, erection and faults by timestamp; align cutter position, wear, thrust and torque with chainage and test clustering by ground type. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b103-v14-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「有效掘進利用率」的交付需回答：以完整停時分類配對地質及刀具檢查，另用班次時間閉合檢查有無重複計時。停機紀錄使用可追溯原因碼，把地質變化與設備故障分開統計，參數調整只能在設備和施工團隊核准程序內進行。","textEn":"For Gotthard Base Tunnel, the effective boring utilisation handover must address the following evidence: Pair downtime classes with geology and cutter inspections, closing shift time to detect double-counting. Use traceable downtime codes, separating geological change from equipment faults; parameter changes stay within procedures approved by equipment and construction teams.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「掘進利用率與設備停時」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","以完整停時分類配對地質及刀具檢查，另用班次時間閉合檢查有無重複計時。","知道覆土深度就能唯一決定洞壁各方向的應力。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Pair downtime classes with geology and cutter inspections, closing shift time to detect double-counting.","Cover depth uniquely determines wall stress in every direction."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以完整停時分類配對地質及刀具檢查，另用班次時間閉合檢查有無重複計時。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Pair downtime classes with geology and cutter inspections, closing shift time to detect double-counting. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":43},{"id":"b103-v14-20","title":"掘進利用率與設備停時：失效診斷","titleEn":"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v14-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「有效掘進利用率」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Effective boring utilisation” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把換刀和出渣重疊時間加兩次會低估利用率，錯誤地支持增購機械的決策。只提高瞬時進尺可能使出渣或刀具超出有效工況，短暫改善後增加停機，平均進尺和零件壽命反而下降。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Double-counting overlapping cutter and spoil delays understates utilisation and can falsely justify more machinery. Higher instantaneous advance can overload cutters or muck transport and create longer stoppages that reduce average progress and component life. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：岩石強度與磨蝕性對刀具的影響不同，混合掌子面又產生不對稱作用；比較機器績效須按地質分區和停時原因分類，不能只排序最高進尺。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Compare performance by ground domain and downtime cause, because the highest short-duration penetration rate can coexist with poor daily production and increased maintenance demand.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「刀盤瞬間轉得更快就保證全工程平均進尺更高。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A faster instantaneous cutterhead speed guarantees higher project-average advance.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v14-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把換刀和出渣重疊時間加兩次會低估利用率，錯誤地支持增購機械的決策。只提高瞬時進尺可能使出渣或刀具超出有效工況，短暫改善後增加停機，平均進尺和零件壽命反而下降。","textEn":"Double-counting overlapping cutter and spoil delays understates utilisation and can falsely justify more machinery. Higher instantaneous advance can overload cutters or muck transport and create longer stoppages that reduce average progress and component life.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b103-v14-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「掘進利用率與設備停時」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Boring utilisation and equipment downtime\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。","把換刀和出渣重疊時間加兩次會低估利用率，錯誤地支持增購機械的決策。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly.","Double-counting overlapping cutter and spoil delays understates utilisation and can falsely justify more machinery."],"answer":2,"explanation":"把換刀和出渣重疊時間加兩次會低估利用率，錯誤地支持增購機械的決策。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Double-counting overlapping cutter and spoil delays understates utilisation and can falsely justify more machinery. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":44},{"id":"b103-v14-21","title":"共享通道與運輸瓶頸：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Shared access and transport bottlenecks: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v14-20"],"objective":"說明「出渣運輸節拍」如何影響哥達基線隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Muck-transport cycle” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Gotthard Base Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"哥達多工作面共用後勤的教學重點是串聯瓶頸，豎井、連絡通道和卸料區的能力不能在不同時間假設下相加。多工作面只有在供電、通風、出渣與材料供應同步充足時才增加總產量。共用豎井或軌道形成串聯瓶頸，排隊和維修窗口會降低名目容量；緩衝區太大又可能侵占通行與救援空間，因此不能單純把各面產能相加。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「出渣運輸節拍」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The multiple-heading context highlights serial logistics bottlenecks: shafts, connecting galleries and unloading areas cannot be combined using inconsistent time assumptions. Multiple headings increase output only when power, air, muck transport and materials support them together. Shared shafts or railways become serial bottlenecks, while queues and maintenance reduce nominal capacity. Large buffers may obstruct personnel and rescue access, so face capacities cannot simply be added without a network-level transport and storage check. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Muck-transport cycle” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：車輛數=4 個；每車載量=22 t；往返週期=35 min。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: vehicles=4 count; payload=22 t; cycle=35 min.","failure":"常見誤解：「增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「出渣運輸節拍」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Muck-transport cycle”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v14-21-k1","title":"共享通道與運輸瓶頸","titleEn":"Shared access and transport bottlenecks","text":"哥達多工作面共用後勤的教學重點是串聯瓶頸，豎井、連絡通道和卸料區的能力不能在不同時間假設下相加。多工作面只有在供電、通風、出渣與材料供應同步充足時才增加總產量。","textEn":"The multiple-heading context highlights serial logistics bottlenecks: shafts, connecting galleries and unloading areas cannot be combined using inconsistent time assumptions. Multiple headings increase output only when power, air, muck transport and materials support them together.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b103-v14-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「共享通道與運輸瓶頸」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Shared access and transport bottlenecks\" is correct?","options":["哥達多工作面共用後勤的教學重點是串聯瓶頸，豎井、連絡通道和卸料區的能力不能在不同時間假設下相加。","增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。","兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。"],"optionsEn":["The multiple-heading context highlights serial logistics bottlenecks: shafts, connecting galleries and unloading areas cannot be combined using inconsistent time assumptions.","Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly.","Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error."],"answer":0,"explanation":"哥達多工作面共用後勤的教學重點是串聯瓶頸，豎井、連絡通道和卸料區的能力不能在不同時間假設下相加。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The multiple-heading context highlights serial logistics bottlenecks: shafts, connecting galleries and unloading areas cannot be combined using inconsistent time assumptions. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":45},{"id":"b103-v14-22","title":"共享通道與運輸瓶頸：定量估算","titleEn":"Shared access and transport bottlenecks: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v14-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「出渣運輸節拍」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Muck-transport cycle” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：車輛數=4 個；每車載量=22 t；往返週期=35 min。C=N payload 60/T=150.857 t/h。僅把往返週期增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為137.143 t/h。邊界：無排隊理想循環，並非共享路段實際產能；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: vehicles=4 count; payload=22 t; cycle=35 min. C=N payload 60/T=150.857 t/h. Increasing only cycle by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 137.143 t/h. Boundary: Ideal cycle without queues, not actual shared-route production. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：對同一日逐小時建立材料和出渣需求表，核對維修時段是否同步占用共用運輸節點。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Build hourly material and spoil demand for the same day and identify maintenance overlap at shared transport nodes.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v14-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：車輛數=4 個；每車載量=22 t；往返週期=35 min。C=N payload 60/T=150.857 t/h。僅把往返週期增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為137.143 t/h。邊界：無排隊理想循環，並非共享路段實際產能；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: vehicles=4 count; payload=22 t; cycle=35 min. C=N payload 60/T=150.857 t/h. Increasing only cycle by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 137.143 t/h. Boundary: Ideal cycle without queues, not actual shared-route production. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b103-v14-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「共享通道與運輸瓶頸」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Shared access and transport bottlenecks\", which statement holds?","options":["動壓公式算出的數值就是長鐵路隧道完整壓力波。","原創教學假設：車輛數=4 個；每車載量=22 t；往返週期=35 min。","基線隧道坡度很小，所以不必做牽引與制動分析。"],"optionsEn":["A dynamic-pressure calculation is the complete pressure-wave prediction for a long rail tunnel.","Original teaching assumptions: vehicles=4 count; payload=22 t; cycle=35 min.","A small base-tunnel gradient eliminates the need for traction and braking analysis."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：車輛數=4 個；每車載量=22 t；往返週期=35 min。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: vehicles=4 count; payload=22 t; cycle=35 min. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":46},{"id":"b103-v14-23","title":"共享通道與運輸瓶頸：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Shared access and transport bottlenecks: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v14-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「出渣運輸節拍」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Muck-transport cycle” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"對同一日逐小時建立材料和出渣需求表，核對維修時段是否同步占用共用運輸節點。以裝載質量、往返時間及排隊時間重建物流曲線，再核對緩衝占用、共用通道優先權與維修時段。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Build hourly material and spoil demand for the same day and identify maintenance overlap at shared transport nodes. Reconstruct flow from payload, round-trip and queue times, then check buffer occupancy, shared-route priorities and maintenance periods. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「出渣運輸節拍」的交付需回答：對同一日逐小時建立材料和出渣需求表，核對維修時段是否同步占用共用運輸節點。每日排程同時標示人員、材料和維修的占用時段，任何物流改線先檢查通風與應變通道，不能只看運量提升。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Gotthard Base Tunnel, the muck-transport cycle handover must address the following evidence: Build hourly material and spoil demand for the same day and identify maintenance overlap at shared transport nodes. Schedules show personnel, materials and maintenance occupancy together; rerouting first checks ventilation and emergency access rather than only throughput gains.","failure":"注意干擾：各面個別達成計畫但共同卸料區壅塞時，整體進度仍可能失守，應由網路而非單面診斷。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Faces may meet local plans while shared unloading congestion defeats overall progress, requiring a network-level diagnosis. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v14-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"對同一日逐小時建立材料和出渣需求表，核對維修時段是否同步占用共用運輸節點。以裝載質量、往返時間及排隊時間重建物流曲線，再核對緩衝占用、共用通道優先權與維修時段。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Build hourly material and spoil demand for the same day and identify maintenance overlap at shared transport nodes. Reconstruct flow from payload, round-trip and queue times, then check buffer occupancy, shared-route priorities and maintenance periods. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b103-v14-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「出渣運輸節拍」的交付需回答：對同一日逐小時建立材料和出渣需求表，核對維修時段是否同步占用共用運輸節點。每日排程同時標示人員、材料和維修的占用時段，任何物流改線先檢查通風與應變通道，不能只看運量提升。","textEn":"For Gotthard Base Tunnel, the muck-transport cycle handover must address the following evidence: Build hourly material and spoil demand for the same day and identify maintenance overlap at shared transport nodes. Schedules show personnel, materials and maintenance occupancy together; rerouting first checks ventilation and emergency access rather than only throughput gains.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「共享通道與運輸瓶頸」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Shared access and transport bottlenecks\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。","對同一日逐小時建立材料和出渣需求表，核對維修時段是否同步占用共用運輸節點。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem.","Build hourly material and spoil demand for the same day and identify maintenance overlap at shared transport nodes."],"answer":2,"explanation":"對同一日逐小時建立材料和出渣需求表，核對維修時段是否同步占用共用運輸節點。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Build hourly material and spoil demand for the same day and identify maintenance overlap at shared transport nodes. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":47},{"id":"b103-v14-24","title":"共享通道與運輸瓶頸：失效診斷","titleEn":"Shared access and transport bottlenecks: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v14-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「出渣運輸節拍」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Muck-transport cycle” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"各面個別達成計畫但共同卸料區壅塞時，整體進度仍可能失守，應由網路而非單面診斷。把理想往返時間當全天常數會忽略交會等待與卸料堵塞，導致工作面停工或把材料堆入必要通道。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Faces may meet local plans while shared unloading congestion defeats overall progress, requiring a network-level diagnosis. Treating an ideal cycle as constant all day misses passing delays and unloading blockages, stopping headings or pushing material into essential access space. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：共用豎井或軌道形成串聯瓶頸，排隊和維修窗口會降低名目容量；緩衝區太大又可能侵占通行與救援空間，因此不能單純把各面產能相加。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Large buffers may obstruct personnel and rescue access, so face capacities cannot simply be added without a network-level transport and storage check.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v14-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"各面個別達成計畫但共同卸料區壅塞時，整體進度仍可能失守，應由網路而非單面診斷。把理想往返時間當全天常數會忽略交會等待與卸料堵塞，導致工作面停工或把材料堆入必要通道。","textEn":"Faces may meet local plans while shared unloading congestion defeats overall progress, requiring a network-level diagnosis. Treating an ideal cycle as constant all day misses passing delays and unloading blockages, stopping headings or pushing material into essential access space.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b103-v14-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「共享通道與運輸瓶頸」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Shared access and transport bottlenecks\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["各面個別達成計畫但共同卸料區壅塞時，整體進度仍可能失守，應由網路而非單面診斷。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Faces may meet local plans while shared unloading congestion defeats overall progress, requiring a network-level diagnosis.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error."],"answer":0,"explanation":"各面個別達成計畫但共同卸料區壅塞時，整體進度仍可能失守，應由網路而非單面診斷。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Faces may meet local plans while shared unloading congestion defeats overall progress, requiring a network-level diagnosis. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":48}],"order":7},{"id":"b103-v14-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「控制網與貫通誤差」與「熱源分配與空氣顯熱」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Control network and breakthrough error\" and \"Heat sources and sensible-air removal\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b103-v14-25","title":"控制網與貫通誤差：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Control network and breakthrough error: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v14-24"],"objective":"說明「方向角誤差」如何影響哥達基線隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Orientation error” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Gotthard Base Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"哥達長距離貫通要區分方向傳遞、尺度及高程三類誤差，地下兩組控制網即使互相閉合，也可能共用同一錯誤地表基準。長隧道的微小方向誤差會沿距離累積，地下控制網又缺少直接衛星定位，必須把地表基準可靠傳到洞內。閉合差很小不代表無系統誤差；尺度、折光、儀器定向與高程基準可能共同偏移，誤差相關性也使平方和估算失真。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「方向角誤差」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Distinguish orientation, scale and elevation errors over long breakthrough distances; two underground networks can close while sharing a wrong surface datum. Small orientation errors accumulate over long drives, while underground networks lack direct satellite positioning and depend on transferring surface control. A small closure does not exclude systematic bias: scale, refraction, orientation and vertical datum may shift together. Correlated errors also invalidate a naive root-sum-square combination of supposedly independent observations. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Orientation error” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：控制長度=3240 m；方向偏角=2.6 arcsec。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: control length=3240 m; orientation error=2.6 arcsec. e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0408407 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「方向角誤差」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Orientation error”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v14-25-k1","title":"控制網與貫通誤差","titleEn":"Control network and breakthrough error","text":"哥達長距離貫通要區分方向傳遞、尺度及高程三類誤差，地下兩組控制網即使互相閉合，也可能共用同一錯誤地表基準。長隧道的微小方向誤差會沿距離累積，地下控制網又缺少直接衛星定位，必須把地表基準可靠傳到洞內。","textEn":"Distinguish orientation, scale and elevation errors over long breakthrough distances; two underground networks can close while sharing a wrong surface datum. Small orientation errors accumulate over long drives, while underground networks lack direct satellite positioning and depend on transferring surface control.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b103-v14-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「控制網與貫通誤差」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Control network and breakthrough error\" is correct?","options":["兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。","哥達長距離貫通要區分方向傳遞、尺度及高程三類誤差，地下兩組控制網即使互相閉合，也可能共用同一錯誤地表基準。","只要體積風量相同，不同海拔的空氣散熱量一定相同。"],"optionsEn":["Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error.","Distinguish orientation, scale and elevation errors over long breakthrough distances; two underground networks can close while sharing a wrong surface datum.","Equal volumetric airflow provides identical cooling at every altitude."],"answer":1,"explanation":"哥達長距離貫通要區分方向傳遞、尺度及高程三類誤差，地下兩組控制網即使互相閉合，也可能共用同一錯誤地表基準。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Distinguish orientation, scale and elevation errors over long breakthrough distances; two underground networks can close while sharing a wrong surface datum. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":49},{"id":"b103-v14-26","title":"控制網與貫通誤差：定量估算","titleEn":"Control network and breakthrough error: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v14-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「方向角誤差」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Orientation error” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：控制長度=3240 m；方向偏角=2.6 arcsec。e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0408407 m。僅把方向偏角增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.0449248 m。邊界：小角度方向偏差，未加入控制網相關性及折光；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: control length=3240 m; orientation error=2.6 arcsec. e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0408407 m. Increasing only orientation error by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.0449248 m. Boundary: Small-angle orientation error without network correlation or refraction. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：獨立重算地表至各工作面的轉換，對照原始角距和不同環境條件量測，保留誤差相關性。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Independently recompute transformations to each heading using raw observations under different conditions, retaining error correlations.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v14-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：控制長度=3240 m；方向偏角=2.6 arcsec。e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0408407 m。僅把方向偏角增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.0449248 m。邊界：小角度方向偏差，未加入控制網相關性及折光；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: control length=3240 m; orientation error=2.6 arcsec. e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0408407 m. Increasing only orientation error by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.0449248 m. Boundary: Small-angle orientation error without network correlation or refraction. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b103-v14-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「控制網與貫通誤差」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Control network and breakthrough error\", which statement holds?","options":["全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。","知道覆土深度就能唯一決定洞壁各方向的應力。","原創教學假設：控制長度=3240 m；方向偏角=2.6 arcsec。"],"optionsEn":["Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.","Cover depth uniquely determines wall stress in every direction.","Original teaching assumptions: control length=3240 m; orientation error=2.6 arcsec. e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0408407 m."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：控制長度=3240 m；方向偏角=2.6 arcsec。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: control length=3240 m; orientation error=2.6 arcsec. e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0408407 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":50},{"id":"b103-v14-27","title":"控制網與貫通誤差：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Control network and breakthrough error: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v14-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「方向角誤差」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Orientation error” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"獨立重算地表至各工作面的轉換，對照原始角距和不同環境條件量測，保留誤差相關性。由獨立測量組複核地表到洞內的轉換，保留原始角距及溫度資料，用不同控制線比較方向與高程偏差。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Independently recompute transformations to each heading using raw observations under different conditions, retaining error correlations. Independently check surface-to-tunnel transformations, retain raw angles, distances and temperatures, and compare orientation and elevation through separate control routes. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「方向角誤差」的交付需回答：獨立重算地表至各工作面的轉換，對照原始角距和不同環境條件量測，保留誤差相關性。貫通前凍結座標、尺度與高程版本，獨立組直接使用原始觀測重算；不得只傳遞整理好的坐標而遺失校正資訊。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Gotthard Base Tunnel, the orientation error handover must address the following evidence: Independently recompute transformations to each heading using raw observations under different conditions, retaining error correlations. Freeze coordinate, scale and height revisions before breakthrough; independent reviewers recompute raw observations rather than receiving only adjusted coordinates without corrections.","failure":"注意干擾：只報一個三維閉合量會掩蓋高程方向的系統偏差，使軌道銜接問題延後暴露。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: One three-dimensional closure magnitude can hide a systematic height bias until track connection. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v14-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"獨立重算地表至各工作面的轉換，對照原始角距和不同環境條件量測，保留誤差相關性。由獨立測量組複核地表到洞內的轉換，保留原始角距及溫度資料，用不同控制線比較方向與高程偏差。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Independently recompute transformations to each heading using raw observations under different conditions, retaining error correlations. Independently check surface-to-tunnel transformations, retain raw angles, distances and temperatures, and compare orientation and elevation through separate control routes. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b103-v14-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「方向角誤差」的交付需回答：獨立重算地表至各工作面的轉換，對照原始角距和不同環境條件量測，保留誤差相關性。貫通前凍結座標、尺度與高程版本，獨立組直接使用原始觀測重算；不得只傳遞整理好的坐標而遺失校正資訊。","textEn":"For Gotthard Base Tunnel, the orientation error handover must address the following evidence: Independently recompute transformations to each heading using raw observations under different conditions, retaining error correlations. Freeze coordinate, scale and height revisions before breakthrough; independent reviewers recompute raw observations rather than receiving only adjusted coordinates without corrections.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「控制網與貫通誤差」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Control network and breakthrough error\"?","options":["獨立重算地表至各工作面的轉換，對照原始角距和不同環境條件量測，保留誤差相關性。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、開挖序列與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。"],"optionsEn":["Independently recompute transformations to each heading using raw observations under different conditions, retaining error correlations.","Temperature, water head, excavation sequence and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure."],"answer":0,"explanation":"獨立重算地表至各工作面的轉換，對照原始角距和不同環境條件量測，保留誤差相關性。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Independently recompute transformations to each heading using raw observations under different conditions, retaining error correlations. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":51},{"id":"b103-v14-28","title":"控制網與貫通誤差：失效診斷","titleEn":"Control network and breakthrough error: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v14-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「方向角誤差」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Orientation error” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只報一個三維閉合量會掩蓋高程方向的系統偏差，使軌道銜接問題延後暴露。共用錯誤基準可能讓兩組測量同時看似一致，直到貫通或軌道銜接才發現系統偏差，修正成本遠高於早期複核。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"One three-dimensional closure magnitude can hide a systematic height bias until track connection. A shared wrong datum can make separate surveys appear consistent until breakthrough or track connection exposes bias that is costly to correct. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：閉合差很小不代表無系統誤差；尺度、折光、儀器定向與高程基準可能共同偏移，誤差相關性也使平方和估算失真。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Correlated errors also invalidate a naive root-sum-square combination of supposedly independent observations.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v14-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只報一個三維閉合量會掩蓋高程方向的系統偏差，使軌道銜接問題延後暴露。共用錯誤基準可能讓兩組測量同時看似一致，直到貫通或軌道銜接才發現系統偏差，修正成本遠高於早期複核。","textEn":"One three-dimensional closure magnitude can hide a systematic height bias until track connection. A shared wrong datum can make separate surveys appear consistent until breakthrough or track connection exposes bias that is costly to correct.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b103-v14-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「控制網與貫通誤差」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Control network and breakthrough error\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","只報一個三維閉合量會掩蓋高程方向的系統偏差，使軌道銜接問題延後暴露。","只要體積風量相同，不同海拔的空氣散熱量一定相同。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","One three-dimensional closure magnitude can hide a systematic height bias until track connection.","Equal volumetric airflow provides identical cooling at every altitude."],"answer":1,"explanation":"只報一個三維閉合量會掩蓋高程方向的系統偏差，使軌道銜接問題延後暴露。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"One three-dimensional closure magnitude can hide a systematic height bias until track connection. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":52},{"id":"b103-v14-29","title":"熱源分配與空氣顯熱：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Heat sources and sensible-air removal: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v14-28"],"objective":"說明「通風顯熱量」如何影響哥達基線隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Ventilation sensible heat” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Gotthard Base Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"哥達深部岩體放熱與列車或施工機械熱源時間尺度不同，需比較穩態空氣熱帳與長期岩體溫度演化，避免把短時試驗當全年能力。深部岩體、列車和機械會向空氣持續放熱，空氣帶走的顯熱由質量流量與溫升決定。相同體積風量在不同密度下不具有相同散熱能力；濕度、岩體瞬變及水冷系統還需分開記帳，單一穩態熱平衡不能預測全部溫度尖峰。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「通風顯熱量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Deep-rock heat evolves on a different timescale from trains or machinery; compare air balances with longer rock-temperature evolution rather than treating short trials as year-round capability. Deep rock, trains and machinery release heat to the air, whose sensible removal depends on mass flow and temperature rise. Equal volumetric flow at different density does not provide equal cooling. Moisture, transient rock heat and water cooling need separate accounts; a steady balance cannot predict every temperature peak or local worker exposure. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Ventilation sensible heat” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；體積風量=84 m³/s；定壓比熱=1.005 kJ/(kg·K)；溫升=15 K。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: air density=1.2 kg/m³; volume flow=84 m³/s; specific heat=1.005 kJ/(kg·K); temperature rise=15 K.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要體積風量相同，不同海拔的空氣散熱量一定相同。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Equal volumetric airflow provides identical cooling at every altitude.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「通風顯熱量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Ventilation sensible heat”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v14-29-k1","title":"熱源分配與空氣顯熱","titleEn":"Heat sources and sensible-air removal","text":"哥達深部岩體放熱與列車或施工機械熱源時間尺度不同，需比較穩態空氣熱帳與長期岩體溫度演化，避免把短時試驗當全年能力。深部岩體、列車和機械會向空氣持續放熱，空氣帶走的顯熱由質量流量與溫升決定。","textEn":"Deep-rock heat evolves on a different timescale from trains or machinery; compare air balances with longer rock-temperature evolution rather than treating short trials as year-round capability. Deep rock, trains and machinery release heat to the air, whose sensible removal depends on mass flow and temperature rise.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b103-v14-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要體積風量相同，不同海拔的空氣散熱量一定相同。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Equal volumetric airflow provides identical cooling at every altitude. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「熱源分配與空氣顯熱」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Heat sources and sensible-air removal\" is correct?","options":["只要體積風量相同，不同海拔的空氣散熱量一定相同。","動壓公式算出的數值就是長鐵路隧道完整壓力波。","哥達深部岩體放熱與列車或施工機械熱源時間尺度不同，需比較穩態空氣熱帳與長期岩體溫度演化，避免把短時試驗當全年能力。"],"optionsEn":["Equal volumetric airflow provides identical cooling at every altitude.","A dynamic-pressure calculation is the complete pressure-wave prediction for a long rail tunnel.","Deep-rock heat evolves on a different timescale from trains or machinery."],"answer":2,"explanation":"哥達深部岩體放熱與列車或施工機械熱源時間尺度不同，需比較穩態空氣熱帳與長期岩體溫度演化，避免把短時試驗當全年能力。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Deep-rock heat evolves on a different timescale from trains or machinery; compare air balances with longer rock-temperature evolution rather than treating short trials as year-round capability. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":53},{"id":"b103-v14-30","title":"熱源分配與空氣顯熱：定量估算","titleEn":"Heat sources and sensible-air removal: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v14-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「通風顯熱量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Ventilation sensible heat” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；體積風量=84 m³/s；定壓比熱=1.005 kJ/(kg·K)；溫升=15 K。Q=ρVcpΔT=1519.56 kW。僅把體積風量增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為1671.52 kW。邊界：僅空氣顯熱，不含濕度潛熱及岩體瞬變；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: air density=1.2 kg/m³; volume flow=84 m³/s; specific heat=1.005 kJ/(kg·K); temperature rise=15 K. Q=ρVcpΔT=1519.56 kW. Increasing only volume flow by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 1671.52 kW. Boundary: Sensible air heat only, excluding latent heat and rock transients. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將岩壁溫度、風量及機械負載分別保存，檢查停工降溫是否真的代表岩體熱源已消失。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Retain wall temperature, airflow and machine load separately and test whether shutdown cooling truly indicates reduced rock heat.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v14-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；體積風量=84 m³/s；定壓比熱=1.005 kJ/(kg·K)；溫升=15 K。Q=ρVcpΔT=1519.56 kW。僅把體積風量增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為1671.52 kW。邊界：僅空氣顯熱，不含濕度潛熱及岩體瞬變；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: air density=1.2 kg/m³; volume flow=84 m³/s; specific heat=1.005 kJ/(kg·K); temperature rise=15 K. Q=ρVcpΔT=1519.56 kW. Increasing only volume flow by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 1671.52 kW. Boundary: Sensible air heat only, excluding latent heat and rock transients. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b103-v14-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「熱源分配與空氣顯熱」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Heat sources and sensible-air removal\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；體積風量=84 m³/s；定壓比熱=1.005 kJ/(kg·K)；溫升=15 K。","基線隧道坡度很小，所以不必做牽引與制動分析。","支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: air density=1.2 kg/m³; volume flow=84 m³/s; specific heat=1.005 kJ/(kg·K); temperature rise=15 K.","A small base-tunnel gradient eliminates the need for traction and braking analysis.","Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；體積風量=84 m³/s；定壓比熱=1.005 kJ/(kg·K)；溫升=15 K。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: air density=1.2 kg/m³; volume flow=84 m³/s; specific heat=1.005 kJ/(kg·K); temperature rise=15 K. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":54},{"id":"b103-v14-31","title":"熱源分配與空氣顯熱：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Heat sources and sensible-air removal: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v14-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「通風顯熱量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Ventilation sensible heat” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將岩壁溫度、風量及機械負載分別保存，檢查停工降溫是否真的代表岩體熱源已消失。同步量測進出口溫濕度、風量及設備負載，分開平均與尖峰時段，用能量收支殘差檢查漏列熱源。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Retain wall temperature, airflow and machine load separately and test whether shutdown cooling truly indicates reduced rock heat. Synchronise inlet/outlet temperature, humidity, flow and equipment load, separate average and peak periods, and use energy residuals to identify missing sources. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「通風顯熱量」的交付需回答：將岩壁溫度、風量及機械負載分別保存，檢查停工降溫是否真的代表岩體熱源已消失。熱帳分別列岩體、交通、機械與水冷路徑，交接時保存季節和負載範圍，設備增設前須重新核對可用散熱能力。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Gotthard Base Tunnel, the ventilation sensible heat handover must address the following evidence: Retain wall temperature, airflow and machine load separately and test whether shutdown cooling truly indicates reduced rock heat. Keep rock, traffic, machinery and water-cooling paths separate; retain seasonal and load ranges and reassess cooling capacity before adding equipment.","failure":"注意干擾：停機後空氣迅速降溫但岩體仍持續放熱，重新載入時可能很快回到高溫，需辨認熱儲存。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Air cools quickly after shutdown while rock retains heat, so renewed loading can rapidly restore high temperatures. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v14-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將岩壁溫度、風量及機械負載分別保存，檢查停工降溫是否真的代表岩體熱源已消失。同步量測進出口溫濕度、風量及設備負載，分開平均與尖峰時段，用能量收支殘差檢查漏列熱源。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Retain wall temperature, airflow and machine load separately and test whether shutdown cooling truly indicates reduced rock heat. Synchronise inlet/outlet temperature, humidity, flow and equipment load, separate average and peak periods, and use energy residuals to identify missing sources. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b103-v14-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「通風顯熱量」的交付需回答：將岩壁溫度、風量及機械負載分別保存，檢查停工降溫是否真的代表岩體熱源已消失。熱帳分別列岩體、交通、機械與水冷路徑，交接時保存季節和負載範圍，設備增設前須重新核對可用散熱能力。","textEn":"For Gotthard Base Tunnel, the ventilation sensible heat handover must address the following evidence: Retain wall temperature, airflow and machine load separately and test whether shutdown cooling truly indicates reduced rock heat. Keep rock, traffic, machinery and water-cooling paths separate; retain seasonal and load ranges and reassess cooling capacity before adding equipment.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「熱源分配與空氣顯熱」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Heat sources and sensible-air removal\"?","options":["沿用另一條隧道或另一處地層的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","將岩壁溫度、風量及機械負載分別保存，檢查停工降溫是否真的代表岩體熱源已消失。","刀盤瞬間轉得更快就保證全工程平均進尺更高。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another tunnel or ground formation counts as verifying this structure.","Retain wall temperature, airflow and machine load separately and test whether shutdown cooling truly indicates reduced rock heat.","A faster instantaneous cutterhead speed guarantees higher project-average advance."],"answer":1,"explanation":"將岩壁溫度、風量及機械負載分別保存，檢查停工降溫是否真的代表岩體熱源已消失。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Retain wall temperature, airflow and machine load separately and test whether shutdown cooling truly indicates reduced rock heat. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":55},{"id":"b103-v14-32","title":"熱源分配與空氣顯熱：失效診斷","titleEn":"Heat sources and sensible-air removal: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v14-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「通風顯熱量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Ventilation sensible heat” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"停機後空氣迅速降溫但岩體仍持續放熱，重新載入時可能很快回到高溫，需辨認熱儲存。把低密度空氣視為海平面空氣會高估散熱，局部熱點也可能被斷面平均溫度掩蓋，導致設備或工作環境超限。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Air cools quickly after shutdown while rock retains heat, so renewed loading can rapidly restore high temperatures. Assuming sea-level density overstates cooling at low density, while cross-sectional averages hide hot spots affecting equipment and the work environment. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：相同體積風量在不同密度下不具有相同散熱能力；濕度、岩體瞬變及水冷系統還需分開記帳，單一穩態熱平衡不能預測全部溫度尖峰。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Moisture, transient rock heat and water cooling need separate accounts; a steady balance cannot predict every temperature peak or local worker exposure.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要體積風量相同，不同海拔的空氣散熱量一定相同。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Equal volumetric airflow provides identical cooling at every altitude.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v14-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"停機後空氣迅速降溫但岩體仍持續放熱，重新載入時可能很快回到高溫，需辨認熱儲存。把低密度空氣視為海平面空氣會高估散熱，局部熱點也可能被斷面平均溫度掩蓋，導致設備或工作環境超限。","textEn":"Air cools quickly after shutdown while rock retains heat, so renewed loading can rapidly restore high temperatures. Assuming sea-level density overstates cooling at low density, while cross-sectional averages hide hot spots affecting equipment and the work environment.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b103-v14-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「熱源分配與空氣顯熱」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Heat sources and sensible-air removal\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","動壓公式算出的數值就是長鐵路隧道完整壓力波。","停機後空氣迅速降溫但岩體仍持續放熱，重新載入時可能很快回到高溫，需辨認熱儲存。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","A dynamic-pressure calculation is the complete pressure-wave prediction for a long rail tunnel.","Air cools quickly after shutdown while rock retains heat, so renewed loading can rapidly restore high temperatures."],"answer":2,"explanation":"停機後空氣迅速降溫但岩體仍持續放熱，重新載入時可能很快回到高溫，需辨認熱儲存。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Air cools quickly after shutdown while rock retains heat, so renewed loading can rapidly restore high temperatures. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":56}],"order":8},{"id":"b103-v14-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「列車壓力波與動壓量級」與「資產編碼與可追溯交接」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Train pressure waves and dynamic-pressure scale\" and \"Asset identity and traceable handover\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b103-v14-33","title":"列車壓力波與動壓量級：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Train pressure waves and dynamic-pressure scale: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v14-32"],"objective":"說明「入口壓力擾動」如何影響哥達基線隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Portal pressure disturbance” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Gotthard Base Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"哥達高速鐵路的氣動檢核需配對列車編組、速度及隧道斷面，對向交會與門位改變會產生不同壓力歷程，不能只看動壓比例。列車進洞壓縮前方空氣，波動在洞口、橫通道和斷面變化處傳播與反射。速度和阻塞比影響壓力量級，但不可壓動壓只是比較尺度，不能替代可壓縮瞬變計算；兩車交會、門位與列車外形都可能改變乘客及設備的壓力歷程。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「入口壓力擾動」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Pair formation, speed and cross-section for aerodynamic assessment; encounters and door states produce different pressure histories beyond simple dynamic-pressure scaling. A train entering a tunnel compresses the air ahead, producing waves reflected at portals, passages and section changes. Speed and blockage influence magnitude, but incompressible dynamic pressure is only a comparison scale, not a compressible transient solution. Train encounters, door states and vehicle shape change the pressure histories experienced by passengers and equipment. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Portal pressure disturbance” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；列車速度=42 m/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: air density=1.2 kg/m³; train speed=42 m/s. q=ρv²/2=1058.4 Pa.","failure":"常見誤解：「動壓公式算出的數值就是長鐵路隧道完整壓力波。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A dynamic-pressure calculation is the complete pressure-wave prediction for a long rail tunnel.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「入口壓力擾動」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Portal pressure disturbance”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v14-33-k1","title":"列車壓力波與動壓量級","titleEn":"Train pressure waves and dynamic-pressure scale","text":"哥達高速鐵路的氣動檢核需配對列車編組、速度及隧道斷面，對向交會與門位改變會產生不同壓力歷程，不能只看動壓比例。列車進洞壓縮前方空氣，波動在洞口、橫通道和斷面變化處傳播與反射。","textEn":"Pair formation, speed and cross-section for aerodynamic assessment; encounters and door states produce different pressure histories beyond simple dynamic-pressure scaling. A train entering a tunnel compresses the air ahead, producing waves reflected at portals, passages and section changes.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b103-v14-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：動壓公式算出的數值就是長鐵路隧道完整壓力波。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A dynamic-pressure calculation is the complete pressure-wave prediction for a long rail tunnel. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「列車壓力波與動壓量級」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Train pressure waves and dynamic-pressure scale\" is correct?","options":["哥達高速鐵路的氣動檢核需配對列車編組、速度及隧道斷面，對向交會與門位改變會產生不同壓力歷程，不能只看動壓比例。","動壓公式算出的數值就是長鐵路隧道完整壓力波。","全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。"],"optionsEn":["Pair formation, speed and cross-section for aerodynamic assessment.","A dynamic-pressure calculation is the complete pressure-wave prediction for a long rail tunnel.","Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted."],"answer":0,"explanation":"哥達高速鐵路的氣動檢核需配對列車編組、速度及隧道斷面，對向交會與門位改變會產生不同壓力歷程，不能只看動壓比例。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Pair formation, speed and cross-section for aerodynamic assessment; encounters and door states produce different pressure histories beyond simple dynamic-pressure scaling. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":57},{"id":"b103-v14-34","title":"列車壓力波與動壓量級：定量估算","titleEn":"Train pressure waves and dynamic-pressure scale: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v14-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「入口壓力擾動」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Portal pressure disturbance” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；列車速度=42 m/s。q=ρv²/2=1058.4 Pa。僅把列車速度增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為1280.66 Pa。邊界：不可壓動壓尺度，不是可壓縮列車壓力波解；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: air density=1.2 kg/m³; train speed=42 m/s. q=ρv²/2=1058.4 Pa. Increasing only train speed by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 1280.66 Pa. Boundary: Incompressible dynamic-pressure scale, not a compressible train pressure-wave solution. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在不同里程同步記錄壓力波抵達時間，以傳播時間和反射時刻檢查模型邊界，而非只擬合峰值。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Record wave arrival at multiple chainages and use propagation and reflection timing to test boundaries rather than fitting peaks alone.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v14-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；列車速度=42 m/s。q=ρv²/2=1058.4 Pa。僅把列車速度增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為1280.66 Pa。邊界：不可壓動壓尺度，不是可壓縮列車壓力波解；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: air density=1.2 kg/m³; train speed=42 m/s. q=ρv²/2=1058.4 Pa. Increasing only train speed by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 1280.66 Pa. Boundary: Incompressible dynamic-pressure scale, not a compressible train pressure-wave solution. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b103-v14-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「列車壓力波與動壓量級」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Train pressure waves and dynamic-pressure scale\", which statement holds?","options":["知道覆土深度就能唯一決定洞壁各方向的應力。","原創教學假設：空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；列車速度=42 m/s。","混凝土強度達標就不必檢查接縫轉動與偏壓。"],"optionsEn":["Cover depth uniquely determines wall stress in every direction.","Original teaching assumptions: air density=1.2 kg/m³; train speed=42 m/s. q=ρv²/2=1058.4 Pa.","Passing concrete strength eliminates the need to check joint rotation and uneven pressure."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；列車速度=42 m/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: air density=1.2 kg/m³; train speed=42 m/s. q=ρv²/2=1058.4 Pa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":58},{"id":"b103-v14-35","title":"列車壓力波與動壓量級：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Train pressure waves and dynamic-pressure scale: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v14-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「入口壓力擾動」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Portal pressure disturbance” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在不同里程同步記錄壓力波抵達時間，以傳播時間和反射時刻檢查模型邊界，而非只擬合峰值。以相同列車編組、速度和門位量測多點壓力歷程，檢查峰值、上升時間及反射抵達時刻，而不只比較一個最大值。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Record wave arrival at multiple chainages and use propagation and reflection timing to test boundaries rather than fitting peaks alone. Measure pressure histories at several points with matching train formation, speed and door states, comparing rise time and reflection arrival as well as peaks. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「入口壓力擾動」的交付需回答：在不同里程同步記錄壓力波抵達時間，以傳播時間和反射時刻檢查模型邊界，而非只擬合峰值。試車報告記錄編組、速度、溫度及門位版本，土建斷面變更與設備耐壓驗證共用同一氣動模型，不能各自選有利情境。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Gotthard Base Tunnel, the portal pressure disturbance handover must address the following evidence: Record wave arrival at multiple chainages and use propagation and reflection timing to test boundaries rather than fitting peaks alone. Trial reports retain formation, speed, temperature and door revisions; civil changes and equipment-pressure checks share one aerodynamic model rather than selectively favourable cases.","failure":"注意干擾：錯誤邊界可能碰巧擬合最大值卻錯估升壓速率，設備承受的循環需求仍會不正確。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: An incorrect boundary may match the peak accidentally while misrepresenting rise rate and cyclic equipment demand. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v14-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在不同里程同步記錄壓力波抵達時間，以傳播時間和反射時刻檢查模型邊界，而非只擬合峰值。以相同列車編組、速度和門位量測多點壓力歷程，檢查峰值、上升時間及反射抵達時刻，而不只比較一個最大值。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Record wave arrival at multiple chainages and use propagation and reflection timing to test boundaries rather than fitting peaks alone. Measure pressure histories at several points with matching train formation, speed and door states, comparing rise time and reflection arrival as well as peaks. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b103-v14-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「入口壓力擾動」的交付需回答：在不同里程同步記錄壓力波抵達時間，以傳播時間和反射時刻檢查模型邊界，而非只擬合峰值。試車報告記錄編組、速度、溫度及門位版本，土建斷面變更與設備耐壓驗證共用同一氣動模型，不能各自選有利情境。","textEn":"For Gotthard Base Tunnel, the portal pressure disturbance handover must address the following evidence: Record wave arrival at multiple chainages and use propagation and reflection timing to test boundaries rather than fitting peaks alone. Trial reports retain formation, speed, temperature and door revisions; civil changes and equipment-pressure checks share one aerodynamic model rather than selectively favourable cases.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「列車壓力波與動壓量級」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Train pressure waves and dynamic-pressure scale\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。","在不同里程同步記錄壓力波抵達時間，以傳播時間和反射時刻檢查模型邊界，而非只擬合峰值。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly.","Record wave arrival at multiple chainages and use propagation and reflection timing to test boundaries rather than fitting peaks alone."],"answer":2,"explanation":"在不同里程同步記錄壓力波抵達時間，以傳播時間和反射時刻檢查模型邊界，而非只擬合峰值。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Record wave arrival at multiple chainages and use propagation and reflection timing to test boundaries rather than fitting peaks alone. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":59},{"id":"b103-v14-36","title":"列車壓力波與動壓量級：失效診斷","titleEn":"Train pressure waves and dynamic-pressure scale: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v14-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「入口壓力擾動」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Portal pressure disturbance” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"錯誤邊界可能碰巧擬合最大值卻錯估升壓速率，設備承受的循環需求仍會不正確。以單一動壓數字當允收值會漏掉壓力梯度與反射疊加，可能使門扇、密封或乘客舒適度需求被低估。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"An incorrect boundary may match the peak accidentally while misrepresenting rise rate and cyclic equipment demand. Using one dynamic-pressure value for acceptance misses gradients and superposed reflections, understating demands on doors, seals or passenger comfort. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：速度和阻塞比影響壓力量級，但不可壓動壓只是比較尺度，不能替代可壓縮瞬變計算；兩車交會、門位與列車外形都可能改變乘客及設備的壓力歷程。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Train encounters, door states and vehicle shape change the pressure histories experienced by passengers and equipment.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「動壓公式算出的數值就是長鐵路隧道完整壓力波。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A dynamic-pressure calculation is the complete pressure-wave prediction for a long rail tunnel.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v14-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"錯誤邊界可能碰巧擬合最大值卻錯估升壓速率，設備承受的循環需求仍會不正確。以單一動壓數字當允收值會漏掉壓力梯度與反射疊加，可能使門扇、密封或乘客舒適度需求被低估。","textEn":"An incorrect boundary may match the peak accidentally while misrepresenting rise rate and cyclic equipment demand. Using one dynamic-pressure value for acceptance misses gradients and superposed reflections, understating demands on doors, seals or passenger comfort.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b103-v14-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「列車壓力波與動壓量級」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Train pressure waves and dynamic-pressure scale\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["錯誤邊界可能碰巧擬合最大值卻錯估升壓速率，設備承受的循環需求仍會不正確。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。"],"optionsEn":["An incorrect boundary may match the peak accidentally while misrepresenting rise rate and cyclic equipment demand.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted."],"answer":0,"explanation":"錯誤邊界可能碰巧擬合最大值卻錯估升壓速率，設備承受的循環需求仍會不正確。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"An incorrect boundary may match the peak accidentally while misrepresenting rise rate and cyclic equipment demand. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":60},{"id":"b103-v14-37","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v14-36"],"objective":"說明「資產資料完整度」如何影響哥達基線隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Asset-record completeness” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Gotthard Base Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"哥達交付從多個施工面整併成一個鐵路資產系統，需把不同承包界面、材料批次及試運轉版本連到同一里程，避免資料在土建與機電間斷裂。地下設備的竣工資料必須讓維護人員找到正確位置、材料批次和控制版本。只有上傳圖面而沒有變更歷程，無法分辨元件替換與真正劣化；告警、儀器、線路及工單使用一致識別碼，才可能把量測趨勢連回實際受力或水力系統。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「資產資料完整度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Integrate multiple construction fronts into one railway asset system, linking contract interfaces, batches and commissioning revisions to chainage so civil and systems evidence remain connected. Handover must let maintainers find the correct location, material batch and control revision. Drawings without change history cannot distinguish replacement from deterioration. Consistent identifiers across alarms, instruments, circuits and work orders are essential for linking trends to the physical structural or hydraulic system instead of treating each record as an isolated file. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Asset-record completeness” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：設備總數=102 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: asset count=102 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=84.3137 %.","failure":"常見誤解：「全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「資產資料完整度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Asset-record completeness”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v14-37-k1","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover","text":"哥達交付從多個施工面整併成一個鐵路資產系統，需把不同承包界面、材料批次及試運轉版本連到同一里程，避免資料在土建與機電間斷裂。地下設備的竣工資料必須讓維護人員找到正確位置、材料批次和控制版本。","textEn":"Integrate multiple construction fronts into one railway asset system, linking contract interfaces, batches and commissioning revisions to chainage so civil and systems evidence remain connected. Handover must let maintainers find the correct location, material batch and control revision.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b103-v14-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「資產編碼與可追溯交接」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Asset identity and traceable handover\" is correct?","options":["全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。","哥達交付從多個施工面整併成一個鐵路資產系統，需把不同承包界面、材料批次及試運轉版本連到同一里程，避免資料在土建與機電間斷裂。","基線隧道坡度很小，所以不必做牽引與制動分析。"],"optionsEn":["Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.","Integrate multiple construction fronts into one railway asset system, linking contract interfaces, batches and commissioning revisions to chainage so civil and systems evidence remain connected.","A small base-tunnel gradient eliminates the need for traction and braking analysis."],"answer":1,"explanation":"哥達交付從多個施工面整併成一個鐵路資產系統，需把不同承包界面、材料批次及試運轉版本連到同一里程，避免資料在土建與機電間斷裂。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Integrate multiple construction fronts into one railway asset system, linking contract interfaces, batches and commissioning revisions to chainage so civil and systems evidence remain connected. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":61},{"id":"b103-v14-38","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接：定量估算","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v14-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「資產資料完整度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Asset-record completeness” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：設備總數=102 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。coverage=100(N−missing)/N=84.3137 %。僅把缺紀錄數增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為82.7451 %。邊界：資料完整度，不等於安全或可靠度；擾動為連續敏感度，實際個數為整數；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: asset count=102 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=84.3137 %. Increasing only missing records by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 82.7451 %. Boundary: Record completeness, not safety or reliability; perturbation is continuous sensitivity while actual counts are integers. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：抽查一段軌道附近設備，將竣工位置、供電路徑和控制版本追至對應施工及試驗紀錄。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Sample equipment near one track section and trace position, supply and control revision to construction and commissioning records.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v14-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：設備總數=102 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。coverage=100(N−missing)/N=84.3137 %。僅把缺紀錄數增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為82.7451 %。邊界：資料完整度，不等於安全或可靠度；擾動為連續敏感度，實際個數為整數；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: asset count=102 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=84.3137 %. Increasing only missing records by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 82.7451 %. Boundary: Record completeness, not safety or reliability; perturbation is continuous sensitivity while actual counts are integers. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b103-v14-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「資產編碼與可追溯交接」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Asset identity and traceable handover\", which statement holds?","options":["支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。","刀盤瞬間轉得更快就保證全工程平均進尺更高。","原創教學假設：設備總數=102 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。"],"optionsEn":["Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem.","A faster instantaneous cutterhead speed guarantees higher project-average advance.","Original teaching assumptions: asset count=102 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=84.3137 %."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：設備總數=102 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: asset count=102 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=84.3137 %. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":62},{"id":"b103-v14-39","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v14-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「資產資料完整度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Asset-record completeness” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"抽查一段軌道附近設備，將竣工位置、供電路徑和控制版本追至對應施工及試驗紀錄。抽取一條告警，從控制畫面追到設備、線路、圖面和工單，核對位置、版本及校正日期並記錄無法閉合的欄位。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Sample equipment near one track section and trace position, supply and control revision to construction and commissioning records. Trace a sampled alarm from screen to equipment, circuit, drawing and work order, checking location, revision and calibration dates and recording broken links. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「資產資料完整度」的交付需回答：抽查一段軌道附近設備，將竣工位置、供電路徑和控制版本追至對應施工及試驗紀錄。交接以可完成的定位、查找與復原任務驗證，由維護責任人確認現場可用性；完整度只是資料指標，不代表結構安全或設備可靠。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Gotthard Base Tunnel, the asset-record completeness handover must address the following evidence: Sample equipment near one track section and trace position, supply and control revision to construction and commissioning records. Validate handover through achievable location, retrieval and recovery tasks witnessed by maintainers; completeness measures records, not structural safety or equipment reliability.","failure":"注意干擾：各標段檔案各自完整但里程原點不同，會讓相鄰設備對不上圖面，維修隔離可能定位錯誤。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Complete contract files with inconsistent chainage origins can mislocate adjacent assets and maintenance isolation. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v14-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"抽查一段軌道附近設備，將竣工位置、供電路徑和控制版本追至對應施工及試驗紀錄。抽取一條告警，從控制畫面追到設備、線路、圖面和工單，核對位置、版本及校正日期並記錄無法閉合的欄位。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Sample equipment near one track section and trace position, supply and control revision to construction and commissioning records. Trace a sampled alarm from screen to equipment, circuit, drawing and work order, checking location, revision and calibration dates and recording broken links. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b103-v14-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「資產資料完整度」的交付需回答：抽查一段軌道附近設備，將竣工位置、供電路徑和控制版本追至對應施工及試驗紀錄。交接以可完成的定位、查找與復原任務驗證，由維護責任人確認現場可用性；完整度只是資料指標，不代表結構安全或設備可靠。","textEn":"For Gotthard Base Tunnel, the asset-record completeness handover must address the following evidence: Sample equipment near one track section and trace position, supply and control revision to construction and commissioning records. Validate handover through achievable location, retrieval and recovery tasks witnessed by maintainers; completeness measures records, not structural safety or equipment reliability.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「資產編碼與可追溯交接」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Asset identity and traceable handover\"?","options":["抽查一段軌道附近設備，將竣工位置、供電路徑和控制版本追至對應施工及試驗紀錄。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Sample equipment near one track section and trace position, supply and control revision to construction and commissioning records.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error."],"answer":0,"explanation":"抽查一段軌道附近設備，將竣工位置、供電路徑和控制版本追至對應施工及試驗紀錄。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Sample equipment near one track section and trace position, supply and control revision to construction and commissioning records. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":63},{"id":"b103-v14-40","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接：失效診斷","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b103-v14-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「資產資料完整度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Asset-record completeness” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"各標段檔案各自完整但里程原點不同，會讓相鄰設備對不上圖面，維修隔離可能定位錯誤。設備改名卻未更新控制畫面會引導人員隔離錯誤回路，材料批次缺漏則使同批缺陷無法追蹤到其他位置。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Complete contract files with inconsistent chainage origins can mislocate adjacent assets and maintenance isolation. Renaming an asset without updating the screen can isolate the wrong circuit; missing material batches prevent tracing related defects at other locations. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：只有上傳圖面而沒有變更歷程，無法分辨元件替換與真正劣化；告警、儀器、線路及工單使用一致識別碼，才可能把量測趨勢連回實際受力或水力系統。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Consistent identifiers across alarms, instruments, circuits and work orders are essential for linking trends to the physical structural or hydraulic system instead of treating each record as an isolated file.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b103-v14-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"各標段檔案各自完整但里程原點不同，會讓相鄰設備對不上圖面，維修隔離可能定位錯誤。設備改名卻未更新控制畫面會引導人員隔離錯誤回路，材料批次缺漏則使同批缺陷無法追蹤到其他位置。","textEn":"Complete contract files with inconsistent chainage origins can mislocate adjacent assets and maintenance isolation. Renaming an asset without updating the screen can isolate the wrong circuit; missing material batches prevent tracing related defects at other locations.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b103-v14-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v7-gotthard-network","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「資產編碼與可追溯交接」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Asset identity and traceable handover\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","各標段檔案各自完整但里程原點不同，會讓相鄰設備對不上圖面，維修隔離可能定位錯誤。","基線隧道坡度很小，所以不必做牽引與制動分析。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Complete contract files with inconsistent chainage origins can mislocate adjacent assets and maintenance isolation.","A small base-tunnel gradient eliminates the need for traction and braking analysis."],"answer":1,"explanation":"各標段檔案各自完整但里程原點不同，會讓相鄰設備對不上圖面，維修隔離可能定位錯誤。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Complete contract files with inconsistent chainage origins can mislocate adjacent assets and maintenance isolation. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":64}],"order":9}],"curriculumVersion":7,"enrichmentVersion":14,"learningTrack":"underground","learningSubdiscipline":"ug-landmarks","learningTags":["underground","ug-landmarks","tunnel"],"subcategory":"ug-landmarks","subcategoryTitle":"世界隧道與地下巨作","subcategoryTitleEn":"World tunnels and underground landmarks","v14Architecture":{"architectureFamily":"tunnel","architectureNodes":[["坡度阻力功率","Grade-resistance power"],["洞壁切向應力","Tangential wall stress"],["襯砌環向壓縮","Lining hoop compression"],["出渣運輸節拍","Muck-transport cycle"],["通風顯熱量","Ventilation sensible heat"],["資產資料完整度","Asset-record completeness"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,5],[1,5]]},"v14Extension":{"stages":5,"steps":40,"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"原創綜合審查：先計算「覆土應力與洞壁重分配」，再獨立計算「共享通道與運輸瓶頸」。原創教學假設：覆土深度=560 m；岩體單位重=26 kN/m³。σθ,max=3γH/1000=43.68 MPa。僅把覆土深度增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為48.048 MPa。邊界：無支承彈性圓孔，僅垂直遠場壓縮且水平遠場應力為零時，側壁最大環向壓應力；不是任意位置應力或完整三維原位解；不是本工程實測或允收值。原創教學假設：車輛數=4 個；每車載量=22 t；往返週期=35 min。C=N payload 60/T=150.857 t/h。僅把往返週期增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為137.143 t/h。邊界：無排隊理想循環，並非共享路段實際產能；不是本工程實測或允收值。兩組結果的單位與邊界不同，不能直接相加。請列出一項缺少的現場輸入，說明它會影響哪個結論，以及哪種獨立量測可以縮小不確定度。","textEn":"Original integrated review: first calculate cover stress and wall redistribution, then independently calculate shared access and transport bottlenecks. Original teaching assumptions: cover=560 m; rock unit weight=26 kN/m³. σθ,max=3γH/1000=43.68 MPa. Increasing only cover by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 48.048 MPa. Boundary: Maximum tangential compression at the sidewalls of an unsupported elastic circular hole under vertical uniaxial remote loading with zero horizontal remote stress; not stress at any point or the complete three-dimensional in-situ state. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Original teaching assumptions: vehicles=4 count; payload=22 t; cycle=35 min. C=N payload 60/T=150.857 t/h. Increasing only cycle by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 137.143 t/h. Boundary: Ideal cycle without queues, not actual shared-route production. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. The outputs have different units and boundaries and cannot simply be added. Identify one missing field input, explain which conclusion it changes and select an independent measurement to reduce uncertainty.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"focus":"深覆土地應力、基線牽引與多工作面整合","focusEn":"Deep-cover stress, base-railway traction and multiple-heading integration"}}};
